D('irritant',{etymology:{"origin":"Irritant is from Latin irritantem, the present participle of irritare, meaning to excite or provoke.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Irritant is from Latin irritantem, the present participle of irritare, meaning to excite or provoke."}],"formationLogic":"Latin present-participle form became an English noun for a thing that provokes irritation.","mnemonic":null,"note":"词源链止于可核实的拉丁语形式；更深层词根不在此断言。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/irritant"},contexts:[{"domain":"医学与环境","senseId":"irritant.s1","en":"Before the clinic approved the new soap, a patch test showed that one ingredient was a skin irritant for several volunteers.","zh":"诊所批准使用这种新肥皂前，斑贴试验显示其中一种成分会刺激几名志愿者的皮肤。","structure":"主句交代 patch test 的结果，that 从句说明 ingredient 的作用。","grammar":"irritant 是可数名词，skin 作前置定语限定刺激发生的部位。","rationale":"这里的 irritant 是引起身体不适的物质，和后文的皮肤反应对应。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The cleaning spray contains a known skin irritant, so the label recommends gloves.','这种清洁喷雾含有已知的皮肤刺激物，因此标签建议戴手套。')],mistakes:[m('The nurse called the smoke a lung irritant and said it irritated the lungs, but then claimed it caused no irritation there.','The nurse called the smoke a lung irritant because it irritated the lungs.','同一句又称烟刺激肺部、又说肺部完全没有受到刺激，两个断言直接冲突。')],quiz:[q('irritant',1,1,'In “Smoke is a lung irritant,” what is an irritant?','Something that causes irritation.','A substance that calms the lungs.','A device that measures lung capacity.','irritant 指会造成刺激或不适的东西。'),q('irritant',2,1,'A skin irritant is most likely to make the skin?','sore or inflamed','immune to every substance','change into a different organ','这里的 irritant 是引发身体刺激反应的物质。'),q('irritant',3,1,'Which could be described as an irritant in an office?','A flickering light that repeatedly distracts staff.','A quiet lamp that works normally.','A chair that supports a worker comfortably.','irritant 也可泛指反复造成烦扰的因素。'),q('irritant',4,1,'Choose the natural phrase.','a chemical irritant','an irritation chemical','an irritate chemical','irritant 可作名词，也可作定语修饰 chemical。')]});
D('irritate',{etymology:{"origin":"Irritate entered English through Latin irritatus, the past participle of irritare, meaning to excite, provoke, or annoy.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Irritate entered English through Latin irritatus, the past participle of irritare, meaning to excite, provoke, or annoy."}],"formationLogic":"The Latin verb developed the bodily-stimulation sense and later the emotional sense of annoying someone.","mnemonic":null,"note":"更深层原始印欧词根说法存在争议，这里只写有把握的拉丁来源。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/irritate"},contexts:[{"domain":"皮肤护理","senseId":"irritate.s2","en":"The detergent may irritate the skin if it is left on the hands for several minutes, so rinse it off promptly.","zh":"如果洗涤剂在手上停留几分钟，可能会刺激皮肤，因此要及时冲洗掉。","structure":"if 从句说明条件，主句给出风险，so 引出建议。","grammar":"may 后接动词原形；it 指代 detergent，left on 是过去分词短语。","rationale":"irritate 在此表示使身体部位疼痛或发炎，而非使人恼火。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The repeated alerts began to irritate staff who were trying to finish the report.','反复弹出的提醒开始惹恼正在赶报告的员工。'),ex(2,'The rough seam irritated the skin beneath his collar.','粗糙的接缝刺激了他衣领下的皮肤。')],mistakes:[m('The wool irritated her skin, but it made the skin completely comfortable and calm.','The wool irritated her skin, and it made the skin sore and uncomfortable.','刺激皮肤通常会带来不适；后半句与 irritate 的身体义相反。')],quiz:[q('irritate',1,1,'A colleague irritates Maya by interrupting her every minute. Maya feels?','annoyed by the repeated interruptions','grateful for the interruptions','physically taller after each interruption','sense 1 指反复惹人烦躁。'),q('irritate',2,2,'A detergent irritates someone’s eyes. What does it do?','makes the eyes sore or uncomfortable','helps the eyes see in darkness','changes the person’s eye colour','sense 2 指使身体部位刺激、疼痛或发炎。'),q('irritate',3,1,'Which sentence uses irritate in the sense of annoying a person?','The constant tapping irritates the passengers.','The cream irritates the cut and makes it sore.','The cold pack numbs the patient’s hand.','对 passengers 的情绪影响对应 sense 1。'),q('irritate',4,2,'Choose the correct sense for a shampoo that irritates the scalp.','It makes the scalp sore or uncomfortable.','It makes the user angry at a delayed bus.','It separates the shampoo from its bottle.','scalp 是身体部位，此处对应刺激身体的 sense 2。')]});
D('irritated',{etymology:{"origin":"Irritated is the past-participle adjective of irritate, a verb borrowed from Latin irritatus and irritare.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Irritated is the past-participle adjective of irritate, a verb borrowed from Latin irritatus and irritare."}],"formationLogic":"The participial adjective describes a person affected by something annoying.","mnemonic":null,"note":"Etymonline 将 irritated 列为 irritate 的相关形式；此处不另推词根。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/irritated"},contexts:[{"domain":"职场沟通","senseId":"irritated.s1","en":"After the third change to the schedule, the usually patient coordinator sounded irritated but still explained the new plan calmly.","zh":"日程第三次变更后，平时很有耐心的协调员听起来有些恼火，但仍平静地解释了新安排。","structure":"时间状语置于句首，but 连接恼火的语气与平静的行动。","grammar":"sound 作系动词，后接形容词 irritated；still 修饰 explained。","rationale":"irritated 描写人的恼火状态，语境将情绪和行为区分开。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The editor sounded irritated when the same typo appeared in the revised draft.','同一个拼写错误又出现在修订稿里时，编辑听起来很恼火。')],mistakes:[m('She was irritated by the delay, meaning she was annoyed and upset; the sentence says she was pleased with the delay.','She was irritated by the delay, meaning she was annoyed and upset.','irritated 表示恼火；wrong 随后却把同一反应说成 pleased。')],quiz:[q('irritated',1,1,'If someone is irritated by a delay, the person is?','annoyed about it','eager to cause the delay','unaware that time has passed','irritated 描述被惹恼、不耐烦的状态。'),q('irritated',2,1,'Which reply sounds irritated?','“I have explained this three times already.”','“Thanks for waiting; I appreciate it.”','“That is wonderful news!”','重复解释后的不耐烦语气体现 irritated。'),q('irritated',3,1,'Choose the correct phrase.','irritated by the noise','irritated from the noise loudly','irritating by the noise','常见结构是 be irritated by something。'),q('irritated',4,1,'A customer gives an irritated sigh. The sigh suggests?','impatience or annoyance','relief and celebration','sleepiness caused only by exercise','irritated 表示恼火，叹气显出不耐烦。')]});
D('island',{etymology:{"origin":"Old English igland or iegland combined ieg, meaning island, with land; its spelling was later influenced by isle.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Old English igland or iegland combined ieg, meaning island, with land; its spelling was later influenced by isle."}],"formationLogic":"The compound originally named land surrounded by water, while the modern spelling reflects later association with isle.","mnemonic":null,"note":"island 的拼写受 isle 影响，但两词来源不同。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/island"},contexts:[{"domain":"道路交通","senseId":"island.s3","en":"At the busy crossing, the children waited on the traffic island until the walk signal appeared on the opposite side.","zh":"在繁忙的路口，孩子们在交通安全岛上等候，直到对面的行人信号灯亮起。","structure":"主句描述等候地点，until 从句说明等待结束的时间点。","grammar":"wait on an island 表示在岛状区域上等候；until 引导时间状语从句。","rationale":"traffic island 是道路中供行人暂候的 raised area，对应词条的交通义项。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The ferry carries fresh food to the island twice a week.','渡船每周两次把新鲜食品运到岛上。'),ex(2,'In the noisy city, the library felt like an island of quiet.','在喧闹的城市里，图书馆像一片宁静的孤岛。'),ex(3,'Pedestrians waited on the traffic island until the crossing signal changed.','行人在人行横道信号变换前等候在交通安全岛上。')],mistakes:[m('The ferry reached the island, a piece of land connected to the mainland on every side.','The ferry reached the island, a piece of land surrounded by water.','岛屿四周被水环绕；四面都与大陆相连不符合 island 的地理义。')],quiz:[q('island',1,1,'A small island is land that is?','surrounded by water','surrounded by mountains but joined to a continent','located entirely underground','sense 1 是四周被水环绕的陆地。'),q('island',2,2,'“An island of calm” in a busy station means?','a small place or situation that feels calm amid activity','a new island built in the sea','a traffic lane reserved for buses','sense 2 是比喻与周围环境不同的一片区域。'),q('island',3,3,'Where might a pedestrian wait on a wide road?','On a raised traffic island between lanes.','In the middle of a moving traffic lane.','On the roof of a nearby building.','sense 3 是供行人短暂停留的道路安全岛。'),q('island',4,1,'Which preposition is standard for living on an island?','on','at','into','常说 live on an island，表示居住在岛上。')]});
D('isle',{etymology:{"origin":"Isle came through Middle English and Old French ile or isle from Latin insula, island; the deeper origin of insula is uncertain.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Isle came through Middle English and Old French ile or isle from Latin insula, island; the deeper origin of insula is uncertain."}],"formationLogic":"The French-derived form survives mainly in literary usage and established place names.","mnemonic":null,"note":"不把 insula 的不确定更深来源写成定论。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/isle"},contexts:[{"domain":"地理与地名","senseId":"isle.s1","en":"Although the isle looked empty from the ferry, a lighthouse keeper and her family lived there throughout the winter.","zh":"尽管从渡船上看这座小岛空无一人，灯塔看守员和她的家人整个冬天都住在那里。","structure":"although 让步从句先给出外观判断，主句随后补充实际居住情况。","grammar":"isle 是 island 的文学或地名式用词；there 回指小岛。","rationale":"本句将 isle 用作普通岛屿名词，语气略带文学色彩。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The guide led us along a narrow path on the Isle of Skye.','导游带我们沿着斯凯岛的一条窄路前行。'),ex(2,'The map labels each isle in the archipelago with a number.','地图用数字标出群岛中的每一座岛。')],mistakes:[m('The travel brochure called it the Isle of Skye, but then spelled the island name “aisle.”','The travel brochure called it the Isle of Skye and spelled the island name “isle.”','isle 指岛，aisle 指过道；专名 Isle of Skye 中应使用 Isle。')],quiz:[q('isle',1,1,'Where is the word isle especially likely to appear?','In a place name such as the Isle of Wight.','In instructions for walking down a supermarket passage.','In a list of cooking measurements.','sense 1 说明 isle 多用于地名或文学表达。'),q('isle',2,2,'In “the British Isles,” what does Isles refer to?','A group of islands.','A row of seats in a theatre.','A chain of mountain peaks.','sense 2 指有名称的群岛中的各座岛。'),q('isle',3,1,'Choose the word for a small island in a poetic description.','isle','aisle','islet only when the name is Isle of Wight','isle 是 island 的文学或地名用法；aisle 意为过道。'),q('isle',4,1,'“They sailed to a distant isle” means they sailed to?','a distant island','a passage between shelves','a distant harbour building','isle 表示岛，常见于文学语境。')]});
D('isolate',{etymology:{"origin":"Isolate was formed in English in 1786 as a back-formation from isolated, which came through French isolé and Italian isolato from Latin insulatus, made into an island.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Isolate was formed in English in 1786 as a back-formation from isolated, which came through French isolé and Italian isolato from Latin insulatus, made into an island."}],"formationLogic":"The verb reanalyzed the participial adjective isolated as a base form meaning to set apart.","mnemonic":null,"note":"意大利语到拉丁语的路径由 Etymonline 所列形式支持。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/isolate"},contexts:[{"domain":"社区生活","senseId":"isolate.s1","en":"When the only bridge closed after the storm, the flooded river temporarily isolated three villages from the nearest hospital.","zh":"暴风雨后唯一的桥关闭时，洪水暂时切断了三个村庄与最近医院之间的联系。","structure":"when 从句设定桥关闭的时间背景，主句说明造成的隔绝结果。","grammar":"isolate + 人或地点 + from 表示使其与某对象隔开；temporarily 修饰动词。","rationale":"此处是地理上使地点与外界隔绝的普通义，不是医学隔离。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'Moving to a new town can isolate older residents who have no local contacts.','搬到新城镇可能使没有当地熟人的老年居民感到孤立。'),ex(2,'The clinic isolated the patient while test results were pending.','检测结果出来前，诊所对这名患者进行了隔离。'),ex(3,'Researchers isolated the active compound from the plant extract.','研究人员从植物提取物中分离出了活性化合物。'),ex(4,'The laboratory compared a virus isolate with two reference samples.','实验室把一株分离病毒与两个参考样本进行了比较。')],mistakes:[m('The lab isolated the compound, meaning it mixed the compound inseparably with every other substance.','The lab isolated the compound, meaning it separated it from the other substances.','科学语境的 isolate 是分离出来；不可分地混在一起表达相反意思。')],quiz:[q('isolate',1,1,'To isolate a person socially is to?','keep the person apart from other people','introduce the person to a larger group','move the person to a nearby seat only','sense 1 指使人或事物与周围分开、孤立。'),q('isolate',2,2,'A clinic isolates a contagious patient in order to?','reduce the chance of spreading infection','help the patient meet more visitors','identify the patient’s favourite food','sense 2 是为控制传染而隔离病人。'),q('isolate',3,3,'Scientists isolate a chemical from a sample by?','separating it from the other components','adding every component together without separation','discarding the sample before testing','sense 3 指从混合物中分离出物质。'),q('isolate',4,4,'In microbiology, an isolate is?','a microorganism or sample separated for study','a room where all laboratory staff meet','the process of blending samples together','sense 4 是供研究的分离菌株或分离样本。')]});
D('isolated',{etymology:{"origin":"Isolated came through French isolé and Italian isolato, from Latin insulatus, literally made into an island; English also uses it as the participle of isolate.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Isolated came through French isolé and Italian isolato, from Latin insulatus, literally made into an island; English also uses it as the participle of isolate."}],"formationLogic":"The island metaphor developed into the adjective meaning kept apart from others.","mnemonic":null,"note":"此处采用词典支持的拉丁—意大利语—法语演变链。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/isolated"},contexts:[{"domain":"乡村地理","senseId":"isolated.s1","en":"The isolated weather station can be reached only by a rough mountain road, and its staff store enough supplies for two weeks.","zh":"这座偏僻的气象站只能沿崎岖山路抵达，工作人员会储备足够两周使用的物资。","structure":"主句说明地点难以抵达，and 连接工作人员的应对措施。","grammar":"isolated 前置修饰 weather station；only 强调唯一交通方式。","rationale":"isolated 在此表示远离其他地点、难以接触，并由山路条件具体体现。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'An isolated farm near the mountain pass receives mail only twice a week.','山口附近一座偏僻农场每周只收两次邮件。')],mistakes:[m('The research samples remained isolated from each other after they were mixed together into one solution.','The research samples were no longer isolated from each other after they were mixed together into one solution.','isolated 表示彼此分开；混成同一溶液后就不再彼此分离。')],quiz:[q('isolated',1,1,'An isolated village is usually?','far from other settlements or difficult to reach','located at the center of a large city','connected to every neighboring village by a busy street','isolated 可表示地理上偏远或与外界隔开。'),q('isolated',2,1,'A person may feel isolated after moving somewhere without friends because the person?','has little contact with others','is surrounded by familiar companions','has decided to host a large party','被隔离也可形容缺少社交联系的感受。'),q('isolated',3,1,'Choose the natural phrase.','an isolated case','an isolating case of yesterday','an isolate case','isolated 是形容词，可修饰 case 表示个别、孤立的案例。'),q('isolated',4,1,'An isolated power failure affected one building only. It was?','limited to that single place','part of a citywide outage','caused by every building failing at once','isolated 也表示个别发生、范围有限。')]});
D('it',{etymology:{"origin":"It descends from Old English hit, a neuter demonstrative pronoun from Proto-Germanic; its h weakened and disappeared in unstressed use.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"It descends from Old English hit, a neuter demonstrative pronoun from Proto-Germanic; its h weakened and disappeared in unstressed use."}],"formationLogic":"An unstressed demonstrative form became the ordinary English pronoun and later the dummy subject in weather clauses.","mnemonic":null,"note":"PIE 祖形的具体重建形式不影响此词条的基本演变，未展开。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/it"},contexts:[{"domain":"天气表达","senseId":"it.s3","en":"It was already snowing when the last bus left the station, so the passengers waited inside until a taxi arrived.","zh":"末班车离站时已经开始下雪，因此乘客们待在室内，直到一辆出租车到来。","structure":"it was snowing 表天气，when 从句定位时间；so 引出结果。","grammar":"天气句中的 it 是形式主语，不指代前文的具体物体。","rationale":"天气表达不需要一个具体施事者，因此 it 占据英语主语位置。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'I found the spare key and put it beside the front door.','我找到了备用钥匙，把它放在前门旁边。'),ex(2,'The baby woke up crying, but it soon settled again.','宝宝醒来哭了起来，但很快又安静下来。'),ex(3,'It is nearly midnight, so we should leave now.','快到午夜了，所以我们现在该走了。'),ex(4,'We found it difficult to hear the guide over the crowd.','人群太吵，我们很难听清导游说话。')],mistakes:[m('The parcel arrived this morning, and I put they on the shelf.','The parcel arrived this morning, and I put it on the shelf.','it 指代前面的单数物品 parcel；they 不能在此代替单数物品。')],quiz:[q('it',1,1,'“I bought a lamp and put it by the bed.” What does it refer to?','the lamp','the bed only','the person who bought it','sense 1 用 it 回指已经提到的事物。'),q('it',2,2,'In “The baby is sleepy; it needs a nap,” it refers to?','the baby','the nap','the speaker’s house','来源列出 it 可指婴儿或性别未知的人。'),q('it',3,3,'In “It is raining,” it functions as?','an empty grammatical subject for weather','a pronoun naming a specific umbrella','the object of the verb rain','sense 3 的 it 作天气表达中的形式主语。'),q('it',4,4,'In “I find it hard to concentrate,” it?','anticipates the later phrase “to concentrate”','refers to a previously named pencil','means the speaker is concentrated','sense 4 的 it 是形式宾语，真正内容由后面的不定式表达。')]});
D('itch',{etymology:{"origin":"Itch continues Old English gicce or giccan and is related to West Germanic forms such as Dutch jeuk and German Juckreiz.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Itch continues Old English gicce or giccan and is related to West Germanic forms such as Dutch jeuk and German Juckreiz."}],"formationLogic":"The inherited Germanic word retained its bodily sensation meaning.","mnemonic":null,"note":"英语、荷兰语和德语的关联由 Etymonline 记载。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/itch"},contexts:[{"domain":"健康与护理","senseId":"itch.s1","en":"The wool collar caused an itch around Nina’s neck, so she changed into a soft cotton shirt before the meeting.","zh":"羊毛衣领让妮娜的脖子周围发痒，所以她在开会前换上了一件柔软的棉衬衫。","structure":"主句说明刺激来源和感觉，so 从句表达由此采取的措施。","grammar":"cause an itch 是名词搭配；around Nina’s neck 指明发痒部位。","rationale":"itch 作可数名词表示皮肤上令人想抓挠的痒感。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The wool blanket made her arms itch, so she changed into a cotton shirt.','羊毛毯让她的手臂发痒，所以她换上了棉衬衫。')],mistakes:[m('The nurse said the bite caused an itch, a tickling feeling on his skin, but his skin had no itching sensation at all.','The nurse said the bite caused an itch, a tickling feeling on his skin.','itch 指皮肤上的刺痒感；wrong 同时说有 itch 和完全没有痒感。')],quiz:[q('itch',1,1,'An itch on your arm is?','an irritating tickling feeling that makes you want to scratch','a sharp sound made by a musical instrument','a mark showing where a bone is broken','itch 作名词指皮肤的刺痒感。'),q('itch',2,1,'If a sweater itches, it?','makes the wearer’s skin feel itchy','fits so loosely that it falls off','keeps the wearer completely dry','itch 作动词可表示使人发痒。'),q('itch',3,1,'“I have an itch to travel” most likely means?','I strongly want to travel.','My skin becomes sore whenever I travel.','I have already bought a travel ticket.','itch 可用于固定表达 an itch to do，表示强烈欲望。'),q('itch',4,1,'Which verb naturally follows “an itch”?','scratch','stir','weigh','人通常会 scratch an itch，即抓挠痒处。')]});
D('item',{etymology:{"origin":"English item comes from Latin item, an adverb meaning likewise or moreover, used to introduce a further point in a list.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"English item comes from Latin item, an adverb meaning likewise or moreover, used to introduce a further point in a list."}],"formationLogic":"A Latin discourse marker for an additional point shifted into a noun naming each listed entry.","mnemonic":null,"note":"拉丁语 item 的拼写与英语形式相同；其词源解释为列举标记。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/item"},contexts:[{"domain":"清单管理","senseId":"item.s1","en":"Each item on the inspection list names one defect, gives its location, and records the date when the repair was completed.","zh":"检查清单上的每一项都列出一处缺陷、注明其位置，并记录维修完成的日期。","structure":"并列的三个谓语 names、gives、records 描述每个条目的信息。","grammar":"each 后接单数名词与单数动词；when 从句修饰 date。","rationale":"item 指清单或集合中的单独一项，句中展示了条目的组成。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The final item on the meeting agenda is the staffing plan.','会议议程的最后一项是人员配置计划。'),ex(2,'Each item of clothing must carry a care label.','每件衣物都必须带有洗护标签。'),ex(3,'The evening news included an item about the bridge closure.','晚间新闻播出了一则关于桥梁封闭的报道。')],mistakes:[m('The receipt listed three item of clothing.','The receipt listed three items of clothing.','three 后的可数名词 item 要用复数 items；of clothing 仍保留单数物质名词。')],quiz:[q('item',1,1,'An item on an agenda is?','one point or subject listed for discussion','the entire meeting room','a person who chairs every meeting','sense 1 指清单或议程中的一个项目。'),q('item',2,2,'At a clothing shop, an item is?','one object or product for sale','a type of shop assistant','a spoken announcement over the radio','sense 2 指一件物品或商品。'),q('item',3,3,'A short report in a broadcast may be called?','a news item','a clothing item','an agenda chair','sense 3 指节目或报刊中的一则内容。'),q('item',4,1,'Complete the phrase: “The next ___ is question time.”','item','items','item of','item 作单数可数名词时用 a/the 或其他限定词；这里 next item 合适。')]});
D('itemise',{etymology:{"origin":"Itemise combines item with the English verbal suffix -ise; the variant itemize uses the spelling -ize.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Itemise combines item with the English verbal suffix -ise; the variant itemize uses the spelling -ize."}],"formationLogic":"The suffix turns the noun item into a verb meaning to set items out one by one.","mnemonic":null,"note":"Etymonline 的 itemize 词条记载该派生；此处保留英式拼写。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/itemize"},contexts:[{"domain":"报销与会计","senseId":"itemise.s1","en":"Please itemise the travel costs on the claim form, separating fares, hotel charges, and meals instead of giving one total.","zh":"请在报销表上逐项列出差旅费用，把车费、酒店费用和餐费分开，而不要只填一个总数。","structure":"祈使句直接提出要求，现在分词短语补充列项方式。","grammar":"itemise 后接被列出的费用；separating 短语解释如何列项。","rationale":"itemise 是英式拼写，表示把整体拆分成清单中的各项。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'Please itemise travel, lodging, and meal costs on the reimbursement form.','请在报销表上逐项列出交通、住宿和餐费。')],mistakes:[m('The clerk itemised the charges, but the bill showed one total and no separate entries.','The clerk totalled the charges, and the bill showed one total with no separate entries.','itemise 指逐项列出；账单没有分项却说已逐项列出，前后矛盾。')],quiz:[q('itemise',1,1,'To itemise expenses is to?','list each expense separately','combine all expenses into one unexplained number','cancel the expenses without recording them','itemise 指把项目逐项列出。'),q('itemise',2,1,'A hotel bill itemises its charges when it?','shows separate amounts for the room, meals, and fees','prints only one total with no details','removes every charge from the bill','逐项显示不同收费项目就是 itemise。'),q('itemise',3,1,'Which spelling is the British form?','itemise','itemize','itemizee','英式拼写 itemise 用 -ise；美式常写 itemize。'),q('itemise',4,1,'Choose the natural construction.','Please itemise the costs by category.','Please itemise about the costs by category.','Please make itemise the costs by category.','itemise 是及物动词，可直接接要列出的内容。')]});
D('its',{etymology:{"origin":"Its arose in late sixteenth-century English from it plus the possessive ending -s, at first often written it's before the apostrophe was dropped.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Its arose in late sixteenth-century English from it plus the possessive ending -s, at first often written it's before the apostrophe was dropped."}],"formationLogic":"The possessive form became orthographically distinct from the contraction it's, meaning it is.","mnemonic":null,"note":"采用历史拼写说明；现代 its 与 it's 必须区分。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/its"},contexts:[{"domain":"机构写作","senseId":"its.s2","en":"The museum changed its opening hours after the conservation team found that visitors needed more time in the galleries.","zh":"修复团队发现参观者需要更多时间逛展厅后，博物馆调整了开放时间。","structure":"after 从句交代调整原因之前发生的发现，that 从句补充发现内容。","grammar":"its 放在名词 opening hours 前作所有格限定词，指 museum。","rationale":"这里的所有者是机构 museum，因此 its 表示机构的开放时间。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The dog carried its bowl to the kitchen.','狗把它的食盆叼到了厨房。'),ex(2,'The museum changed its opening hours for the winter.','博物馆调整了冬季开放时间。')],mistakes:[m('The company updated it’s policy after the review.','The company updated its policy after the review.','表示“它的”要用 its；it’s 是 it is 或 it has 的缩写。')],quiz:[q('its',1,1,'In “The bird built its nest,” its means?','the nest belongs to the bird','the bird is the nest','the bird has built something unrelated','its 是物主限定词，表示“它的”。'),q('its',2,2,'In “The university revised its rules,” whose rules were revised?','the university’s rules','the student’s rules only','the rules of a nearby city','机构名词也可用 its 指其所属。'),q('its',3,1,'Choose the word meaning “belonging to it.”','its','it’s','its’','its 表示所属；it’s 是缩写，its’ 不是标准拼法。'),q('its',4,1,'Complete the sentence: “The engine stopped because ___ fuel line was blocked.”','its','it’s','itself','燃油管属于 engine，需用物主限定词 its。')]});
D('itself',{etymology:{"origin":"Itself is the reflexive form built from Old English hit, it, and self; the combined form was established by late Middle English.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Itself is the reflexive form built from Old English hit, it, and self; the combined form was established by late Middle English."}],"formationLogic":"The pronoun it combines with self to mark that the action returns to the nonhuman subject.","mnemonic":null,"note":"词形沿袭英语反身代词构成；没有额外词缀分析。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/itself"},contexts:[{"domain":"设备说明","senseId":"itself.s1","en":"The thermostat switches itself off when the room reaches the selected temperature, preventing the heater from running all night.","zh":"房间达到设定温度时，恒温器会自动关闭，从而避免加热器整夜运行。","structure":"when 从句说明触发条件，preventing 短语说明关闭带来的结果。","grammar":"itself 回指主语 thermostat；switch itself off 是反身结构，主语和宾语同指。","rationale":"句中的 itself 表示设备对自身执行关闭动作，而不是强调设备本身。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The cat cleaned itself after coming in from the rain.','猫从雨里进屋后自己清理了身体。'),ex(2,'The route itself is simple, although the weather may be difficult.','路线本身很简单，不过天气可能不太好。'),ex(3,'The printer switches itself off after ten minutes of inactivity.','打印机闲置十分钟后会自动关机。')],mistakes:[m('The robot examined itself, and the engineers examined it itself after the test.','The robot examined itself, and the engineers examined it after the test.','反身代词 itself 回指主语 robot；第二分句中的宾语 it 不需要再接 itself。')],quiz:[q('itself',1,1,'In “The puppy scratched itself,” itself shows that?','the puppy and the scratched animal are the same','another puppy did the scratching','the puppy scratched a person','sense 1 是主语与宾语同一事物的反身用法。'),q('itself',2,2,'“The painting itself is valuable” emphasizes?','the painting as the particular thing being discussed','the painter’s house rather than the painting','the frame only, not the artwork','sense 2 用 itself 强调事物本身。'),q('itself',3,3,'“The door closed itself” most likely means it?','closed automatically or without someone closing it','was closed by a different door','could not move at all','sense 3 可表示自动发生或不靠外力完成。'),q('itself',4,1,'Choose the correct reflexive form: “The machine repaired ___.”','itself','its','themselves','machine 是单数事物，反身代词用 itself。')]});
D('ivory',{etymology:{"origin":"Ivory passed from Anglo-French ivorie and Old North French ivurie through Medieval Latin eborium to Latin ebur, elephant ivory.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Ivory passed from Anglo-French ivorie and Old North French ivurie through Medieval Latin eborium to Latin ebur, elephant ivory."}],"formationLogic":"The European forms trace the material name to Latin; any earlier African or Phoenician source remains uncertain.","mnemonic":null,"note":"更早的非洲语或腓尼基语来源只是推测，因此明确保留不确定性。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/ivory"},contexts:[{"domain":"野生动物保护","senseId":"ivory.s1","en":"Because elephants are protected by law, the customs officer confiscated the carved ivory and opened an investigation into its origin.","zh":"由于大象受法律保护，海关官员没收了雕刻象牙制品，并着手调查其来源。","structure":"because 从句说明法律背景，主句并列交代没收和调查。","grammar":"ivory 作物质名词修饰 carved；its 指被没收的象牙制品。","rationale":"句中 ivory 指象牙材料，说明为什么相关制品会触发执法调查。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The museum keeps the carved ivory under glass and documents its legal history.','博物馆把雕刻象牙制品放在玻璃柜中，并记录其合法来源历史。'),ex(2,'She chose an ivory blouse to match the pale flowers in the print.','她选了一件象牙白衬衫，搭配印花上的浅色花朵。'),ex(3,'The old piano has ivory-coloured keys made from modern composite material.','这架旧钢琴的琴键呈象牙色，但由现代复合材料制成。')],mistakes:[m('The dealer described the blue cotton fabric as ivory-coloured.','The dealer described the creamy-white cotton fabric as ivory-coloured.','ivory-coloured 指乳白色；把蓝色改为 creamy-white 后，描述与棉布颜色相符。')],quiz:[q('ivory',1,1,'Ivory in its material sense is?','the hard substance that forms an elephant’s tusks','a soft plant fibre used to make cotton shirts','a blue dye made from sea water','sense 1 指形成象牙的硬质材料。'),q('ivory',2,2,'An ivory dress is described as?','a pale creamy-white colour','a bright green colour','a dress made from paper receipts','sense 2 包括象牙色；现代语境通常指颜色而非材料。'),q('ivory',3,3,'An ivory-coloured keyboard has keys that are?','creamy white in appearance','necessarily carved from elephant tusks','transparent like glass','sense 3 的形容词义可指乳白色，不代表材质真是象牙。'),q('ivory',4,1,'Why should a writer identify the source of an antique ivory object?','Because ivory trade is legally restricted in many contexts.','Because every ivory-coloured object is illegal.','Because ivory can only refer to a paint shade.','源词条提示现代法律限制象牙贸易；实物象牙需注意来源与法规。')]});
D('jab',{etymology:{"origin":"Jab is recorded as a Scottish variant of job, meaning a sharp thrust or blow; job’s own deeper origin is uncertain and may be imitative.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Jab is recorded as a Scottish variant of job, meaning a sharp thrust or blow; job’s own deeper origin is uncertain and may be imitative."}],"formationLogic":"The short sharp sound and motion are compatible with an expressive formation, but the derivation is not certain.","mnemonic":null,"note":"Etymonline 对 job 的更深来源使用可能性措辞，故不把拟声说法当定论。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/jab"},contexts:[{"domain":"疫苗接种","senseId":"jab.s1","en":"The nurse gave Leo a quick jab in the upper arm, then asked him to stay in the clinic for ten minutes.","zh":"护士在利奥上臂迅速打了一针，然后让他在诊所停留十分钟。","structure":"then 连接注射和随后观察两项按顺序发生的动作。","grammar":"give someone a jab 是口语中打针的说法；in the upper arm 标明部位。","rationale":"jab 在这里是注射的一针，词条也涵盖快速戳击这一相关名词义。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The nurse gave him a quick jab before he left the clinic.','他离开诊所前，护士给他快速打了一针。')],mistakes:[m('The clinic recorded a jab, a quick injection, although the nurse did not inject anything.','The clinic recorded a jab, a quick injection given by the nurse.','jab 在医疗场景可指注射；记录了一针却明确说没有注射，彼此冲突。')],quiz:[q('jab',1,1,'A nurse gives a patient a jab. In this context, a jab is?','an injection','a written prescription','a blood-pressure reading','jab 在医疗口语中可指一针或疫苗注射。'),q('jab',2,1,'A boxer throws a jab by making?','a quick straight punch','a slow circular kick','a defensive block with the knee','jab 也指快速短促的拳击。'),q('jab',3,1,'If someone jabs a button with a finger, the person?','pushes it sharply and quickly','polishes it for several minutes','removes it from the panel','动词 jab 表示快速、用力地戳或捅。'),q('jab',4,1,'Which description best fits a jab?','a brief, sharp thrust or hit','a long, gentle massage','a slow walk around a room','词条核心义概括为短促尖锐的一击或一针。')]});
D('jack',{etymology:{"origin":"The lifting device called a jack was named from the familiar male name Jack, which became a generic name for a common fellow and then for mechanical helpers.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"The lifting device called a jack was named from the familiar male name Jack, which became a generic name for a common fellow and then for mechanical helpers."}],"formationLogic":"The device name developed by comparing the tool with an assistant that performs lifting work; the personal name’s ultimate origin is disputed.","mnemonic":null,"note":"人名 Jack 的更早来源有不同解释，这里只说明工具名的可证发展路径。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/Jack"},contexts:[{"domain":"汽车维修","senseId":"jack.s1","en":"Before changing the tire, the driver placed a jack beneath the frame and checked that the car was stable on level ground.","zh":"更换轮胎前，驾驶员把千斤顶放在车架下面，并确认汽车在平地上稳定。","structure":"before 介词短语说明操作顺序，that 从句是 checked 的宾语。","grammar":"place a jack beneath something 描述千斤顶支撑位置；checked that 引导宾语从句。","rationale":"这里的 jack 是把汽车顶起的机械装置。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'Before changing the tyre, he placed a jack beneath the car’s frame.','换轮胎前，他把千斤顶放在车架下方。')],mistakes:[m('She used a jack to lower the car, but the device raised it higher off the ground.','She used a jack to raise the car higher off the ground.','千斤顶的作用是顶起车辆；描述其降低车辆与此用途相反。')],quiz:[q('jack',1,1,'A car jack is used to?','lift part of a car off the ground','measure the tyre pressure','lock the car doors remotely','jack 作名词指用于顶起车辆的装置。'),q('jack',2,1,'Where should a driver place a jack before changing a wheel?','under a suitable lifting point on the car','on top of the windscreen','inside the fuel tank','千斤顶需要置于车辆合适的支撑/顶升点下方。'),q('jack',3,1,'The mechanic jacked up the car. What happened?','The car was raised for repair.','The car’s radio was turned off.','The mechanic removed the road beneath it.','动词短语 jack up 表示用千斤顶顶起。'),q('jack',4,1,'Which item is closest in function to a jack when lifting a vehicle?','a lifting device','a seat belt','a windscreen wiper','jack 的核心用途是举升车辆。')]});
D('jacket',{etymology:{"origin":"Jacket entered English through Middle French or Old French jaquet, a short coat with sleeves, a diminutive of jaque.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Jacket entered English through Middle French or Old French jaquet, a short coat with sleeves, a diminutive of jaque."}],"formationLogic":"The French diminutive named a shorter garment; the older history of jaque is uncertain.","mnemonic":null,"note":"jaque 的远源存在争议，不把某一种盔甲解释说成定论。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/jacket"},contexts:[{"domain":"服装与气候","senseId":"jacket.s1","en":"She kept a light jacket in her backpack because the coastal wind became cold as soon as the sun went behind the clouds.","zh":"她在背包里放了一件薄夹克，因为太阳一躲到云后，海边的风就会变冷。","structure":"because 从句说明携带夹克的原因；as soon as 表示气温变化发生的时点。","grammar":"keep something in a bag 表示随身携带；light 在此修饰 jacket，指薄、轻便。","rationale":"jacket 是短外套，适合挡住海边转冷的风。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'He hung his wet jacket near the heater until the sleeves were dry.','他把湿夹克挂在暖气旁，直到袖子干透。')],mistakes:[m('She wore jacket over her shirt on the cold walk.','She wore a jacket over her shirt on the cold walk.','单数可数名词 jacket 前需要限定词 a。')],quiz:[q('jacket',1,1,'A jacket is generally?','a short coat worn on the upper body','a pair of trousers worn on the legs','a covering placed only over a pillow','来源义项将 jacket 定义为较短的外套。'),q('jacket',2,1,'Which weather might make a light jacket useful?','a cool, breezy afternoon','a very hot day when no extra layer is needed','an underwater dive without protective equipment','夹克是上身外套，凉爽天气可作一层衣物。'),q('jacket',3,1,'Choose the natural phrase.','a leather jacket','a jacket of leathering','a jacketly leather','材料名词 leather 可直接修饰 jacket。'),q('jacket',4,1,'If a jacket is too small, the wearer may?','find it tight across the shoulders','use it to measure the room temperature','wear it as a pair of shoes','jacket 是穿在上身的衣物，尺码会影响肩部合身度。')]});
D('jail',{etymology:{"origin":"Jail came through Middle English and Old French jaiole from Medieval Latin gabiola and Late Latin caveola, a diminutive of cavea, cage or enclosure.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Jail came through Middle English and Old French jaiole from Medieval Latin gabiola and Late Latin caveola, a diminutive of cavea, cage or enclosure."}],"formationLogic":"The word’s history preserves the image of a small enclosed place; gaol is an alternate spelling from the g-form.","mnemonic":null,"note":"拼写 gaol 是历史变体，不是错误形式。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/jail"},contexts:[{"domain":"司法与法律","senseId":"jail.s1","en":"The suspect was held in jail overnight while investigators checked the travel records that could confirm his account.","zh":"调查人员核查可能证实其说法的旅行记录时，嫌疑人被关押在监狱过夜。","structure":"while 从句说明羁押期间正在进行的调查，that 从句修饰 records。","grammar":"be held in jail 是被动结构，表示被关押；could confirm 修饰 records 的证明作用。","rationale":"jail 指羁押人员的场所，不等同于句中作为行动者的 investigators。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The court sent the repeat offender to jail for six months.','法院判这名屡犯者入狱六个月。')],mistakes:[m('The court jailed the defendant, allowing him to leave the prison whenever he wished.','The court jailed the defendant, keeping him in prison for the sentence.','to jail someone 是将其监禁；随时自由离开与监禁矛盾。')],quiz:[q('jail',1,1,'A person in jail is?','being kept in prison','working as a judge in court','waiting at a railway station','jail 作名词指监狱或被关押的状态。'),q('jail',2,1,'If a judge jails someone, the judge?','orders that person to be imprisoned','releases the person from every charge','asks the person to join a jury','jail 作动词表示把人关进监狱。'),q('jail',3,1,'Choose the natural phrase in American English.','spend time in jail','spend time into jail','spend a jail of time','常说 spend time in jail，表示坐牢。'),q('jail',4,1,'Which spelling is a British variant of jail?','gaol','goal','gail','gaol 是 jail 的旧式英式拼写变体，不应与 goal 混淆。')]});
D('jam',{etymology:{"origin":"The fruit spread jam is connected with the verb jam, to press or force tightly together; the verb’s deeper origin is unknown and may relate to Middle English cham.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"The fruit spread jam is connected with the verb jam, to press or force tightly together; the verb’s deeper origin is unknown and may relate to Middle English cham."}],"formationLogic":"The food sense reflects fruit pressed or cooked into a thick mass, though the exact historical path is not fully settled.","mnemonic":null,"note":"jam 动词的来源不确定；果酱义与挤压、压紧的联想不宜写成绝对结论。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/jam"},contexts:[{"domain":"食品制作","senseId":"jam.s1","en":"After the berries had simmered with sugar, Mira poured the thick jam into warm jars and labeled each one with the date.","zh":"浆果和糖炖煮后，米拉把浓稠的果酱倒入温热的罐子，并给每罐贴上日期标签。","structure":"after 从句先交代制作阶段，主句包含倒入和贴标签两个动作。","grammar":"jam 在此为不可数食品名词；each one 回指一个个装好的罐子。","rationale":"句中 thick jam 明确是果酱义，而非道路拥堵或机械卡住的义项。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'She spread raspberry jam on warm toast for breakfast.','她早餐时把覆盆子果酱抹在热吐司上。'),ex(1,'A delivery truck jammed the narrow street during the morning rush.','早高峰时，一辆送货卡车堵住了狭窄街道。')],mistakes:[m('The traffic jam cleared the road and let every car pass freely.','The traffic jam blocked the road and forced cars to move slowly.','traffic jam 指交通堵塞，会妨碍车辆通行，不会让车辆畅通。')],quiz:[q('jam',1,1,'Strawberry jam is?','a sweet fruit spread','a kind of bread knife','a container for hot tea','jam 的食物义是水果制成的甜酱。'),q('jam',2,1,'A traffic jam means?','vehicles are crowded and moving slowly or not at all','the road is empty and clear','traffic lights are permanently removed','jam 的堵塞义描述车辆拥挤、通行受阻。'),q('jam',3,1,'If a drawer jams, it?','gets stuck and will not move smoothly','opens more easily than usual','changes into a storage shelf','动词 jam 可表示卡住、堵塞。'),q('jam',4,1,'Which phrase most clearly means “果酱”?','a jar of apricot jam','a jammed printer tray','a traffic jam at noon','a jar of ... jam 是食品义；另两个指堵塞。')]});
D('jan',{etymology:{"origin":"Jan is the conventional three-letter calendar abbreviation of January, whose name comes through French from Latin Ianuarius, the month sacred to Janus.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Jan is the conventional three-letter calendar abbreviation of January, whose name comes through French from Latin Ianuarius, the month sacred to Janus."}],"formationLogic":"This clipped written form shortens the month name for calendars and dates; it is not an independent ancient word.","mnemonic":null,"note":"月份缩写的形成是现代书写约定；这里的历史词源指向完整词 January。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/January"},contexts:[{"domain":"日历缩写","senseId":"jan.s1","en":"The appointment book marks the inspection as Jan 14, but the clerk added the year because the form will be filed next summer.","zh":"预约簿把检查日期标为1月14日，但职员补上了年份，因为表格要到明年夏天才归档。","structure":"but 连接简写日期与补充年份的理由，because 从句给出原因。","grammar":"Jan 是 January 的常用月份缩写；日期后补年份以消除时间歧义。","rationale":"该例展示 jan 在日期中充当月份标签的缩写，而不是完整月份词。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The calendar marks the conference as “Jan 12,” using the standard month abbreviation.','日历上把会议标为“Jan 12”，采用了标准月份缩写。')],mistakes:[m('The report is dated “Jan 12” and says the meeting took place in July.','The report is dated “Jan 12” and says the meeting took place in January.','Jan 是 January 的缩写；若日期写 Jan 12，正文却说会议在 July，月份信息冲突。')],quiz:[q('jan',1,1,'In a calendar heading, Jan is short for?','January','June','July','jan/Jan 是 January 的截短形式。'),q('jan',2,1,'Which date heading uses the usual English capitalization?','Jan 8','jan 8','JANuary 8','月份缩写通常首字母大写，写作 Jan。'),q('jan',3,1,'A planner shows “Jan–Mar.” Which period does that cover?','January through March','June through August','July through September','Jan 表示 January，是一月的缩写。'),q('jan',4,1,'Choose the standard abbreviation for January.','Jan.','Jany.','Janu','常见英语日期格式用 Jan. 缩写 January。')]});
