D('jargon',{etymology:{"origin":"Jargon entered English from Old French jargon, originally bird chattering or idle talk; its deeper formation is usually treated as echoic.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Jargon entered English from Old French jargon, originally bird chattering or idle talk; its deeper formation is usually treated as echoic."}],"formationLogic":"The word shifted from meaningless or hard-to-follow chatter to specialized vocabulary outsiders may not understand.","mnemonic":null,"note":"拟声来源属于词典给出的解释，未进一步推定更早词根。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/jargon"},contexts:[{"domain":"专业沟通","senseId":"jargon.s1","en":"Because the manual was written for new volunteers, the engineer replaced technical jargon with a diagram and a plain-language explanation.","zh":"由于手册是写给新志愿者的，工程师用示意图和通俗说明替换了专业行话。","structure":"because 从句说明读者对象，主句交代为提升可读性而进行的修改。","grammar":"replace A with B 表示用 B 替换 A；technical 修饰 jargon。","rationale":"jargon 指外行难懂的专业用语，这里通过面向新手的改写体现。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The engineer replaced the technical jargon with plain language for the public notice.','工程师把技术行话改成了通俗表达，用在面向公众的通知上。')],mistakes:[m('The guide avoided jargon by filling every sentence with terms that only specialists understood.','The guide used jargon by filling every sentence with terms that only specialists understood.','只有专家理解的专门术语正是 jargon；说避免行话与后半句矛盾。')],quiz:[q('jargon',1,1,'Jargon is?','specialized language that may be hard for outsiders to understand','a list of ordinary words arranged alphabetically','a short story told to entertain children','jargon 指外行人不易理解的专门用语。'),q('jargon',2,1,'Why might a public-service leaflet remove jargon?','To make the information easier for non-specialists to understand.','To make the leaflet longer without adding information.','To hide the service’s opening hours.','面向公众时减少行话可提高可理解性。'),q('jargon',3,1,'Choose the natural phrase.','legal jargon','a jargon of lawyerses','jargons of legal','jargon 通常作不可数名词，legal jargon 是自然搭配。'),q('jargon',4,1,'A report full of unexplained technical terms is likely full of?','jargon','small talk','punctuation','难懂的专业词汇是 jargon。')]});
D('javelin',{etymology:{"origin":"Javelin came through Old French javeline, a diminutive of javelot, probably from a Celtic source related to a word for a forked branch.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Javelin came through Old French javeline, a diminutive of javelot, probably from a Celtic source related to a word for a forked branch."}],"formationLogic":"The diminutive named a light throwing spear; the proposed Celtic and deeper root connections remain qualified.","mnemonic":null,"note":"凯尔特语及更深原始印欧联系都属于推测，保留 probably。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/javelin"},contexts:[{"domain":"田径运动","senseId":"javelin.s1","en":"After the official checked the throwing sector, the athlete ran up smoothly and sent the javelin beyond the previous day’s mark.","zh":"裁判检查投掷扇区后，运动员平稳助跑，将标枪投过了前一天的成绩标记。","structure":"after 从句交代比赛流程，and 连接助跑与投掷两个动作。","grammar":"send an object beyond a mark 表示将物体投过某个距离标记。","rationale":"javelin 是田径投掷的长矛状器械，不是一般搏斗用刀枪。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The athlete’s javelin landed inside the marked sector, close to the far line.','运动员的标枪落在标定扇形区域内，靠近远端界线。')],mistakes:[m('The athlete called the javelin a heavy ball rolled down a lane.','The athlete called the javelin a long spear-shaped object thrown for distance.','javelin 指运动中投掷的长矛状器械，不是沿跑道滚动的重球。')],quiz:[q('javelin',1,1,'In athletics, a javelin is?','a long spear-shaped object thrown for distance','a heavy ball rolled down a lane','a short stick used only for jumping','javelin 指标枪运动中投掷的长矛状器械。'),q('javelin',2,1,'An athlete competing in the javelin event tries to?','throw the javelin as far as possible within the rules','run while carrying a ball across a line','jump over a bar without touching it','标枪比赛的核心动作是投掷标枪。'),q('javelin',3,1,'Which verb most naturally goes with javelin in sport?','throw','stir','shelve','标枪通常用 throw 投掷。'),q('javelin',4,1,'A javelin landed in the sector. What has happened?','The thrown spear-shaped implement landed in the marked area.','A runner finished a lap in the stadium.','A swimmer reached the far side of a pool.','投掷落入有效区域是标枪比赛的情境。')]});
D('jaw',{etymology:{"origin":"Jaw is recorded in Middle English as jowe or joue, from Old French joue; its more remote source is disputed, with Germanic and Celtic suggestions.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Jaw is recorded in Middle English as jowe or joue, from Old French joue; its more remote source is disputed, with Germanic and Celtic suggestions."}],"formationLogic":"The word entered through French, but the sound history makes proposed deeper connections uncertain.","mnemonic":null,"note":"远源存在不同假说；只将中古英语和古法语阶段作为较可靠来源。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/jaw"},contexts:[{"domain":"医疗检查","senseId":"jaw.s1","en":"The dentist asked Omar to open his jaw slowly, then examined the hinge near the ear before taking an X-ray.","zh":"牙医让奥马尔慢慢张开下颌，然后在拍X光前检查了耳朵附近的关节。","structure":"then 连接检查步骤，before 短语表示拍片前完成触诊。","grammar":"open one’s jaw 表示张开下颌；near the ear 修饰 hinge 的位置。","rationale":"jaw 指围绕口腔的下颌骨结构，本句把它放在口腔检查场景中。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The dentist asked him to relax his jaw before checking the painful tooth.','牙医检查疼痛的牙齿前，请他放松下颌。')],mistakes:[m('After the fall, his jaw hurt, but he felt the pain only in his ankle.','After the fall, his jaw hurt, and the pain was around his mouth.','jaw 指嘴周围的下颌骨；若疼痛只在脚踝，就不能称为 jaw hurt。')],quiz:[q('jaw',1,1,'Your jaw is the bone area?','around your mouth','at the back of your knee','inside your chest','jaw 指嘴周围的下颌骨。'),q('jaw',2,1,'If a person clenches their jaw, they tighten the area around the?','mouth and teeth','ankles and feet','shoulders and elbows','咬紧牙关会收紧下颌周围肌肉。'),q('jaw',3,1,'Choose the natural collocation.','a broken jaw','a jaw of the elbow','a jawed mouthbone','jaw 可与 broken 连用，表示下颌骨骨折。'),q('jaw',4,1,'After chewing for a long time, someone may feel pain in the?','jaw','wrist','heel','咀嚼会活动下颌，长时间咀嚼可能使 jaw 疲劳。')]});
D('jaws',{etymology:{"origin":"Jaws is the regular plural of jaw, a Middle English word from Old French joue; the deeper origin of jaw remains uncertain.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Jaws is the regular plural of jaw, a Middle English word from Old French joue; the deeper origin of jaw remains uncertain."}],"formationLogic":"The plural ending marks the paired gripping parts or mouth bones; no separate etymology is needed for jaws.","mnemonic":null,"note":"保留 jaw 的来源不确定性；复数形式本身是规则屈折。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/jaw"},contexts:[{"domain":"安全设备","senseId":"jaws.s1","en":"During the dental examination, the dentist checked the alignment of both jaws because the patient felt pain whenever he chewed.","zh":"牙科检查时，牙医检查了上下颌的咬合情况，因为患者每次咀嚼都会感到疼痛。","structure":"because 从句解释检查咬合的原因，whenever 从句指出疼痛反复出现的条件。","grammar":"jaws 是 jaw 的复数形式，both 明确表示口腔上下两块颌骨。","rationale":"这里 jaws 直接指口腔两侧的颌骨，病人咀嚼时疼痛与颌部对应。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The crocodile’s jaws closed around the fish before it disappeared underwater.','鳄鱼的上下颌合拢咬住鱼，随后潜入水下。')],mistakes:[m('The shark opened its jaws, revealing its mouth remained completely shut.','The shark opened its jaws, revealing the inside of its mouth.','jaws 张开意味着嘴部打开；说嘴完全闭合与之矛盾。')],quiz:[q('jaws',1,1,'A shark opens its jaws. What does it open?','The bones around its mouth.','The bones around its knees.','The doors of a boat cabin.','jaws 是 jaw 的复数，指口部的上下颌。'),q('jaws',2,1,'“The jaws of a trap” refers to?','the parts that close in and catch something','the trap’s painted instructions','the bait placed outside the trap','jaws 可比喻像上下颌一样合拢的夹口部分。'),q('jaws',3,1,'Which sentence uses the plural form correctly?','The dog’s jaws were strong.','The dog’s jawes were strong.','The dog’s jaw was strongs.','jaw 的复数形式是 jaws。'),q('jaws',4,1,'When someone’s jaws drop in surprise, their mouth?','opens wide','becomes invisible','moves behind their ears','jaws drop 是形容因惊讶而张开嘴的表达。')]});
D('jazz',{etymology:{"origin":"Jazz first appears in early twentieth-century American slang, first in baseball and soon in music; a connection with jasm, energy or spirit, has been proposed but is uncertain.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Jazz first appears in early twentieth-century American slang, first in baseball and soon in music; a connection with jasm, energy or spirit, has been proposed but is uncertain."}],"formationLogic":"The word’s early slang history is documented, while its ultimate origin is unresolved.","mnemonic":null,"note":"关于 jasm 的联系只作一种推测，不将其写作确证词源。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/jazz"},contexts:[{"domain":"音乐与排练","senseId":"jazz.s1","en":"The quartet kept the melody recognizable while the pianist improvised a new rhythm that gave the jazz performance more energy.","zh":"四重奏在保留旋律辨识度的同时，让钢琴手即兴创作了新节奏，为爵士演出增添活力。","structure":"while 从句表达伴随关系，that 从句修饰 rhythm 并说明效果。","grammar":"improvise 是爵士乐常见表现方式；give something energy 是使之更有活力。","rationale":"jazz 在此指包含摇摆、即兴等特点的音乐，而非某种泛指热闹的风格。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The trio improvised a slow jazz piece while the audience listened quietly.','三重奏乐队即兴演奏了一首舒缓的爵士乐曲，观众安静地聆听。')],mistakes:[m('The band played jazz, but every note was fixed in advance and no musician could improvise.','The band played jazz, and the musicians improvised parts of the performance.','即兴演奏是爵士乐的重要特征之一；完全不许即兴与这里的描述不合。')],quiz:[q('jazz',1,1,'Jazz is a style of music often associated with?','swing rhythms and improvisation','spoken dialogue without rhythm','instruments that cannot produce sound','来源义项将 jazz 描述为带摇摆节奏和即兴的音乐。'),q('jazz',2,1,'A jazz musician improvises by?','creating or varying music during the performance','playing only a recording made by someone else','stopping whenever the melody changes','improvise 指演奏中即兴创作或变化。'),q('jazz',3,1,'Choose the natural phrase for a group playing jazz.','a jazz band','a jazz of band','a jazzes band','jazz 可作名词定语修饰 band。'),q('jazz',4,1,'Which venue is most likely to feature a live jazz set?','a small music club with a trio performing','a silent archive with no performances','a swimming pool during a race','爵士乐现场演出常见于音乐俱乐部。')]});
D('jealous',{etymology:{"origin":"Jealous came from Old French jalos or gelos, from Late Latin zelosus, from Latin zelus and Greek zelos, zeal or jealousy.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Jealous came from Old French jalos or gelos, from Late Latin zelosus, from Latin zelus and Greek zelos, zeal or jealousy."}],"formationLogic":"The borrowed adjective developed from a Greek-Latin family associated with ardor and strong desire.","mnemonic":null,"note":"不把更深的 PIE 来源说法写成确定事实。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/jealous"},contexts:[{"domain":"人际关系","senseId":"jealous.s1","en":"Maya felt jealous when her colleague received the award, although she congratulated him and later asked how he had prepared.","zh":"同事获奖时，玛雅感到嫉妒，尽管她还是向他道贺，后来还询问他如何准备。","structure":"when 从句说明情绪触发点，although 从句呈现与情绪并存的礼貌行动。","grammar":"feel jealous 是系动词加形容词；when 引导时间兼背景从句。","rationale":"jealous 表示因别人拥有自己想要的东西而嫉妒，语境交代了对象和反应。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'He felt jealous of his colleague’s promotion, even though they remained friends.','尽管两人仍是朋友，他还是嫉妒同事得到了晋升。')],mistakes:[m('Mia was jealous of her teammate’s award, yet she had no wish to receive that award or anything similar.','Mia was jealous of her teammate’s award because she wished she could have a similar award herself.','jealous 的来源义是想要别人拥有的东西；wrong 却说她完全不想得到它或类似东西。')],quiz:[q('jealous',1,1,'Someone jealous of a friend’s new job may?','wish they had the opportunity or success too','be unable to remember the friend’s name','have hired the friend for the job','jealous 表示嫉妒别人拥有或得到的东西。'),q('jealous',2,1,'Choose the usual preposition.','jealous of her success','jealous on her success','jealous at her success','常说 be jealous of someone/something。'),q('jealous',3,1,'Which situation best illustrates jealous?','A sibling resents the attention another child receives.','A sibling congratulates another child without envy.','A sibling forgets where the family lives.','嫉妒常因他人获得关注或拥有自己想要的东西而起。'),q('jealous',4,1,'Jealous and envious are closest when a person?','wants something another person has','is completely indifferent to others’ possessions','has given away everything they own','jealous 的来源释义就是想要别人拥有的东西。')]});
D('jealousy',{etymology:{"origin":"Jealousy came through Old French jalousie, which could mean enthusiasm, love, longing, or jealousy, from jalos, jealous.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Jealousy came through Old French jalousie, which could mean enthusiasm, love, longing, or jealousy, from jalos, jealous."}],"formationLogic":"The noun developed from the adjective family and historically covered watchful concern as well as envy.","mnemonic":null,"note":"旧义包括关切或警觉，不把它简化为现代单一情绪来源。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/jealousy"},contexts:[{"domain":"心理与沟通","senseId":"jealousy.s1","en":"Rather than hide her jealousy, Lina told her sister that she feared losing their closeness after the move.","zh":"莉娜没有掩饰嫉妒，而是告诉姐姐，她害怕搬家后两人的亲密关系会变淡。","structure":"rather than 引出对照选择，that 从句说明嫉妒背后的担忧。","grammar":"jealousy 是 fear 的宾语；after the move 说明她担心的时间背景。","rationale":"jealousy 名词概括这种强烈不安或嫉妒情绪，本句细化了情绪的来源。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'Open discussion helped prevent jealousy from damaging the sisters’ friendship.','坦诚沟通避免了嫉妒破坏姐妹之间的友谊。')],mistakes:[m('His jealousy made him want his colleague’s award, but he did not want that award or anything similar.','His jealousy made him want an award like the one his colleague had received.','jealousy 是想要别人拥有的东西；wrong 同时说想要又明确说不想要。')],quiz:[q('jealousy',1,1,'Jealousy is the feeling of?','wanting what another person has','being certain that nobody owns anything','being unable to recognize familiar faces','jealousy 指嫉妒、眼红他人所有的情绪。'),q('jealousy',2,1,'In “Jealousy strained their friendship,” what caused tension?','one person’s envy of what the other had','a shared plan that both welcomed','a sudden change in the weather','jealousy 会因嫉妒而损害人际关系。'),q('jealousy',3,1,'Which form is usually used for the emotion as a general idea?','jealousy','a jealousy','jealousies in every sentence','jealousy 通常作不可数抽象名词。'),q('jealousy',4,1,'The phrase “out of jealousy” means?','because of envy','because of gratitude','because of hunger','out of jealousy 表示出于嫉妒。')]});
D('jeans',{etymology:{"origin":"Jeans is the plural of jean, a mid-fifteenth-century name for twilled cotton cloth, shortened from French jean fustian, cloth of Genoa.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Jeans is the plural of jean, a mid-fifteenth-century name for twilled cotton cloth, shortened from French jean fustian, cloth of Genoa."}],"formationLogic":"The fabric name referred to Genoese cloth; the trousers sense is much later, and the cloth was not originally necessarily blue.","mnemonic":null,"note":"牛仔裤义晚于布料名；不把蓝色当作词源特征。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/jean"},contexts:[{"domain":"服装与历史","senseId":"jeans.s1","en":"The museum displayed work jeans from the nineteenth century beside a note explaining how Genoese twilled cloth influenced the garment’s name.","zh":"博物馆在一旁陈列着十九世纪的劳动牛仔裤，并附注说明热那亚斜纹布如何影响了这种服装的名称。","structure":"beside a note 交代展陈方式，how 从句作 explaining 的宾语。","grammar":"jeans 通常以复数形式指裤子；work 作前置定语说明用途。","rationale":"此处 jeans 指由坚韧棉布制成的裤子，词源注释关联 jean 布料和热那亚。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'He wore a pair of dark jeans to the workshop because they were sturdy and easy to wash.','他穿了一条深色牛仔裤去车间，因为这种裤子结实且容易清洗。')],mistakes:[m('She bought one jeans and tried it on in the changing room.','She bought a pair of jeans and tried them on in the changing room.','jeans 通常以复数形式使用；表示一条要说 a pair of jeans，代词也用 them。')],quiz:[q('jeans',1,1,'Jeans are usually?','trousers made from strong cotton denim','a type of cotton shirt with no sleeves','shoes with metal soles','jeans 指牛仔裤，通常以复数形式出现。'),q('jeans',2,1,'How do you normally count one garment called jeans?','a pair of jeans','one jean in everyday use','a jeans','通常说 a pair of jeans 来数一条牛仔裤。'),q('jeans',3,1,'Choose the standard sentence.','These jeans are too long for me.','This jeans is too long for me.','These jeans is too long for me.','jeans 形式为复数，谓语通常用 are。'),q('jeans',4,1,'Which material is most closely associated with jeans?','denim','silk lace','rubber','常见牛仔裤以 denim 牛仔布制成。')]});
D('jeep',{etymology:{"origin":"Jeep is recorded in 1941 U.S. military slang, often linked to the initials G.P. for General Purpose and influenced by Popeye’s character Eugene the Jeep.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Jeep is recorded in 1941 U.S. military slang, often linked to the initials G.P. for General Purpose and influenced by Popeye’s character Eugene the Jeep."}],"formationLogic":"The vehicle name’s history involves both acronym interpretation and popular-culture influence, so neither is presented as the sole certain source.","mnemonic":null,"note":"首字母缩写解释并非唯一无争议来源，保留 Etymonline 所述的双重影响。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/Jeep"},contexts:[{"domain":"野外行车","senseId":"jeep.s1","en":"The rescue crew drove a jeep along the rocky track because the smaller vehicle could reach the stranded hikers where the van could not.","zh":"救援队驾驶吉普车沿着岩石路行驶，因为这辆较小的车能到达面包车无法抵达的地方，把受困徒步者接出来。","structure":"because 从句说明选择车辆的原因，where 从句限定救援地点。","grammar":"jeep 是车辆名词；could reach 与 could not 对比两种车辆能力。","rationale":"jeep 指坚固的越野车，句中突出崎岖路况下的通过能力。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The guide drove a sturdy jeep along the rocky track to the campsite.','向导开着一辆结实的吉普车，沿着多岩石的小路驶向营地。')],mistakes:[m('The jeep was designed for off-road travel, making it suitable only for smooth roads and unsuitable for rough terrain.','The jeep was designed for off-road travel, making it suitable for rough terrain.','越野车用于崎岖地形；wrong 却说它只适合平整道路。')],quiz:[q('jeep',1,1,'A jeep is generally?','a small sturdy vehicle suited to rough roads','a high-speed train for city commuters','a sailing boat used only on calm lakes','来源义项把 jeep 定义为小型结实的越野车。'),q('jeep',2,1,'Which trip is most likely to use a jeep?','driving over a rough track to a remote camp','taking a subway beneath a city','crossing an ocean in a passenger ship','越野车适合崎岖道路和偏远地点。'),q('jeep',3,1,'Which phrase is natural?','a four-wheel-drive jeep','a jeep of four-wheel drivingly','a four-wheel jeep drive','jeep 可由 four-wheel-drive 修饰，形成自然名词短语。'),q('jeep',4,1,'Why might an expedition choose a jeep?','Its sturdy design can handle uneven terrain.','It is designed to travel underwater.','It runs only on railway tracks.','越野车的结实结构适合不平整地形。')]});
D('jelly',{etymology:{"origin":"Jelly came through Middle English gelee from Old French gelee, the past participle of geler, to freeze, from Latin gelare.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Jelly came through Middle English gelee from Old French gelee, the past participle of geler, to freeze, from Latin gelare."}],"formationLogic":"The food name preserves the idea of a liquid setting or freezing into a soft solid.","mnemonic":null,"note":"此处取拉丁 gelare 的冷凝义链，不扩写不确定的更深词根。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/jelly"},contexts:[{"domain":"食品制作","senseId":"jelly.s1","en":"The cook left the berry liquid to cool in shallow dishes, where it set into a clear jelly that could be sliced for dessert.","zh":"厨师把浆果汁留在浅盘中冷却，结果凝成了透明果冻，可以切片作甜点。","structure":"where 从句说明液体冷却凝固的位置，that 从句修饰 jelly。","grammar":"set into 表示凝固成；could be sliced 是被动结构，说明成品状态。","rationale":"jelly 指冷却后凝固的柔软食品，本句说明从液体变成果冻的过程。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The children spooned orange jelly into small cups and left it to set.','孩子们把橙味果冻舀进小杯，放着让它凝固。')],mistakes:[m('The jelly remained liquid in the fridge, yet it had set into a firm shape.','The jelly remained liquid in the fridge and did not set into a firm shape.','jelly 应凝固成形；wrong 同时说仍是液体又凝固成形。')],quiz:[q('jelly',1,1,'Jelly as a dessert is?','a soft food that sets into a firm shape','a dry powder that cannot be mixed with water','a metal container for fruit','来源义项指凝固成胶状的软食。'),q('jelly',2,1,'If jelly has set, it has?','become firm enough to hold its shape','turned into steam','remained completely liquid','set 在此指食物凝固成形。'),q('jelly',3,1,'Which phrase matches the source entry?','grape jelly','jelly of grapeses','a jellys of grape','grape jelly 是自然搭配；jelly 可作不可数或可数。'),q('jelly',4,1,'In American English, jelly may also refer to a fruit spread similar to?','jam','mustard','vinegar','来源备注提到美式英语 jelly 也可指果酱类抹酱。')]});
D('jeopardize',{etymology:{"origin":"Jeopardize adds -ize to jeopardy; jeopardy comes from Old French jeu parti, an even or divided game, which came to imply uncertainty and danger.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Jeopardize adds -ize to jeopardy; jeopardy comes from Old French jeu parti, an even or divided game, which came to imply uncertainty and danger."}],"formationLogic":"The suffix forms a verb meaning to put something into the risky condition named by jeopardy.","mnemonic":null,"note":"jeu parti 的字面解释和风险义历史有关；不将其拆成英语前缀。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/jeopardize"},contexts:[{"domain":"风险管理","senseId":"jeopardize.s1","en":"Skipping the final equipment check could jeopardize the launch, even though every earlier test has produced reliable results.","zh":"即使此前每次测试结果都可靠，跳过最后的设备检查仍可能危及发射。","structure":"even though 从句承认前期成功，主句强调尚存的风险。","grammar":"could 后接动词原形；jeopardize 后接受到威胁的对象 the launch。","rationale":"jeopardize 是使某事处于危险中的动词，句中以可能失去发射安全为风险。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'Sharing the unreleased figures could jeopardize the company’s negotiations.','泄露尚未发布的数据可能危及公司的谈判。')],mistakes:[m('The leak jeopardized the negotiations, making the deal safer and less likely to fail.','The leak jeopardized the negotiations, making the deal less secure and more likely to fail.','jeopardize 意为使处于风险中；让交易更安全与之相反。')],quiz:[q('jeopardize',1,1,'To jeopardize a plan is to?','put it at risk','guarantee that it will succeed','write it down for later','jeopardize 的核心义是危及、使处于危险之中。'),q('jeopardize',2,1,'Which action could jeopardize a confidential deal?','publishing the private terms before signing','keeping the terms restricted to the negotiating team','checking the figures with an authorized adviser','泄露保密条款会使交易面临风险。'),q('jeopardize',3,1,'Choose the correct construction.','jeopardize someone’s safety','jeopardize to someone’s safety','jeopardize about someone’s safety','jeopardize 是及物动词，后面直接接受影响的对象。'),q('jeopardize',4,1,'Which spelling is the British variant?','jeopardise','jeopardizee','jeoperdize','英式英语常把 jeopardize 写作 jeopardise。')]});
D('jerk',{etymology:{"origin":"Jerk for a sudden pull or movement is recorded from the late sixteenth century; its origin is uncertain, with possible links to imitative forms or Middle English variants.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Jerk for a sudden pull or movement is recorded from the late sixteenth century; its origin is uncertain, with possible links to imitative forms or Middle English variants."}],"formationLogic":"The word may imitate a sharp motion or sound, but historical sources do not establish a single derivation.","mnemonic":null,"note":"拟声或中古英语来源只是可能解释；避免把任何一条写成定论。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/jerk"},contexts:[{"domain":"机械与动作","senseId":"jerk.s1","en":"The starter cord gave a sudden jerk when the engine caught, so Priya released it before it pulled her hand toward the casing.","zh":"发动机启动时，拉绳突然猛地一拽，因此普里娅在它把自己的手扯向外壳前松开了绳子。","structure":"when 从句标明猛拉发生时点，so 连接动作后果，before 从句说明松手时机。","grammar":"give a jerk 是名词搭配；it 指 starter cord，pulled 后接宾语和方向短语。","rationale":"jerk 在此是突然而有力的拉动这一名词义。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'A sudden jerk of the steering wheel sent the car toward the curb.','方向盘突然一猛拉，汽车便冲向路缘。')],mistakes:[m('He gave the rope a gentle jerk, pulling it slowly and smoothly with no sudden movement.','He gave the rope a sharp jerk, pulling it suddenly.','jerk 是突然、短促的猛拉；缓慢平顺、没有突然动作与该义矛盾。')],quiz:[q('jerk',1,1,'A jerk of a rope is?','a sudden sharp pull','a slow release of tension over an hour','a knot tied without pulling','jerk 作名词指突然猛的一下或猛拉。'),q('jerk',2,1,'If a driver jerks the wheel, the driver?','moves it suddenly and sharply','polishes it until it shines','removes it from the car permanently','jerk 作动词表示突然猛动、猛拉。'),q('jerk',3,1,'Which verb phrase is natural?','give the rope a jerk','make the rope a jerking','do a jerk to the rope of','自然搭配是 give something a jerk。'),q('jerk',4,1,'A train starts with a jerk when it?','moves off suddenly with a sharp movement','glides smoothly without any movement','stays parked all day','with a jerk 描述突然、颠簸的动作。')]});
D('jersey',{etymology:{"origin":"The garment name jersey comes from knitted cloth associated with Jersey in the Channel Islands; the island name’s own origin is disputed.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"The garment name jersey comes from knitted cloth associated with Jersey in the Channel Islands; the island name’s own origin is disputed."}],"formationLogic":"A place name for the cloth extended to garments made from that material, while the place-name etymology remains unsettled.","mnemonic":null,"note":"海峡群岛地名的来源有竞争解释，故不进一步断言。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/jersey"},contexts:[{"domain":"体育服装","senseId":"jersey.s1","en":"Because the team colors were hard to see under the stadium lights, each player wore a numbered jersey with a bright white back.","zh":"由于在体育场灯光下很难看清队服颜色，每位球员都穿着背面亮白、印有号码的运动衫。","structure":"because 从句提供可见度问题，主句说明服装的设计应对。","grammar":"each player 后用单数 wore；with a bright white back 修饰 jersey。","rationale":"jersey 在此指运动队穿的针织上衣，不是地名本身。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The goalkeeper wore a bright yellow jersey that made her easy to spot.','守门员穿着一件亮黄色运动衫，很容易被人认出来。')],mistakes:[m('The player changed into a jersey, then put on the same jersey over the first one without changing shirts.','The player changed into a clean jersey after taking off the old one.','change into 表示换上另一件衣服；把同一件衣服再套一遍没有表达更换。')],quiz:[q('jersey',1,1,'A team jersey is?','a sports shirt worn by a player','a hard helmet worn on the head','a pair of shoes worn on the feet','来源义项把 jersey 解释为运动衫或球衣。'),q('jersey',2,1,'Which person is most likely to wear a jersey during a match?','a team player','a referee’s desk','a spectator’s bicycle','球员常在比赛中穿队服 jersey。'),q('jersey',3,1,'Choose the natural phrase.','a red team jersey','a red jerseying team','a jersey of redly team','颜色形容词可直接修饰 jersey。'),q('jersey',4,1,'A player swaps jerseys after a match. The player swaps?','sports shirts','tickets for train seats','shoes for gloves','jersey 指运动上衣，赛后交换球衣是常见情景。')]});
D('jest',{etymology:{"origin":"Jest entered English through Old French geste, a tale or exploit, from Latin gesta, things done; the word later narrowed toward a humorous remark.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Jest entered English through Old French geste, a tale or exploit, from Latin gesta, things done; the word later narrowed toward a humorous remark."}],"formationLogic":"The historical sense moved from an account of notable deeds to a playful story or remark.","mnemonic":null,"note":"词义演变路径依 Etymonline 的古法语和拉丁语形式。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/jest"},contexts:[{"domain":"日常交谈","senseId":"jest.s1","en":"He made the remark in jest to ease the tension, but he apologized when he realized that his colleague had taken it seriously.","zh":"他开那个玩笑是为了缓和紧张气氛，但意识到同事当真后便道了歉。","structure":"but 连接玩笑目的和意外结果，when 从句说明道歉的触发时点。","grammar":"in jest 是固定表达，意为开玩笑地；that 从句作 realized 的宾语。","rationale":"jest 指玩笑或逗趣的话，句中通过误解显示玩笑需要结合听者反应。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'Her comment about the muddy boots was made in jest, and everyone laughed.','她关于泥靴的评论是开玩笑说的，大家都笑了。')],mistakes:[m('He said in jest that the team had won, but he was completely serious and not joking.','He said in jest that the team had won, although the team had actually lost.','in jest 表示开玩笑地；声称完全认真、不在开玩笑与该短语矛盾。')],quiz:[q('jest',1,1,'A remark made in jest is made?','as a joke','as a legal order','as a private address','in jest 表示开玩笑地、非认真地。'),q('jest',2,1,'Which sentence uses jest naturally?','She meant the teasing remark in jest.','She jested the chair into the room.','They bought three jests of bread.','jest 常作名词，in jest 是自然固定表达。'),q('jest',3,1,'If someone says “I was only jesting,” they mean?','I was joking.','I was measuring something.','I was making a formal promise.','jest 也可作动词，表示说笑、开玩笑。'),q('jest',4,1,'A jest is closest to a?','joke or funny remark','serious warning issued by a court','list of items for sale','来源义项把 jest 解释为 joke 或逗趣的话。')]});
D('jester',{etymology:{"origin":"Jester comes from Middle English gestour or jestour, a minstrel or reciter, from gesten, to tell a tale, related to geste.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Jester comes from Middle English gestour or jestour, a minstrel or reciter, from gesten, to tell a tale, related to geste."}],"formationLogic":"The older performer who recited stories became the comic entertainer associated with a court.","mnemonic":null,"note":"词义从讲故事者发展为宫廷逗乐者；不与现代口语 joke 混作唯一来源。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/jester"},contexts:[{"domain":"历史剧场","senseId":"jester.s1","en":"The jester interrupted the royal banquet with a clever rhyme, and the guests laughed before the musicians began the next song.","zh":"弄臣用一句巧妙的押韵打断了王室宴席，宾客们笑了起来，随后乐师开始演奏下一首曲子。","structure":"and 连接插话和宾客反应，before 标明后续节目开始时间。","grammar":"interrupt A with B 表示用 B 打断 A；began the next song 是 before 从句。","rationale":"jester 指受雇娱乐他人的表演者，押韵和逗笑宾客体现其职责。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'In the historical play, the jester used songs and jokes to entertain the king.','在这出历史剧中，弄臣用歌谣和笑话逗国王开心。')],mistakes:[m('The jester was hired to amuse the court, but he refused to entertain anyone and only issued tax bills.','The jester was hired to amuse the court by telling jokes and performing.','jester 是受雇逗乐的人；完全不娱乐而只发税单与角色职责不符。')],quiz:[q('jester',1,1,'A jester in a historical court was hired to?','amuse the ruler and people at court','collect crops from every farm','record court judgments as a judge','jester 指受雇在宫廷中逗乐的人。'),q('jester',2,1,'Which character is most likely to be a jester?','a performer who entertains a king with jokes','a guard whose only task is to lock the gates','a clerk who files tax returns','逗乐国王的表演者符合 jester 的历史义。'),q('jester',3,1,'Choose the correct plural.','jesters','jesteres','jester','jester 的规则复数为 jesters。'),q('jester',4,1,'A modern writer might use jester to describe someone who?','acts like a comic entertainer','repairs watches professionally','directs traffic at a crossing','jester 可用于历史角色，也可比喻滑稽逗乐的人。')]});
D('jesus',{etymology:{"origin":"The English name Jesus came through Greek Iēsous and Late Latin Iesus, rendering Aramaic Yeshua or Jeshua, from Hebrew Yehoshua, commonly interpreted as Yahweh is salvation.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"The English name Jesus came through Greek Iēsous and Late Latin Iesus, rendering Aramaic Yeshua or Jeshua, from Hebrew Yehoshua, commonly interpreted as Yahweh is salvation."}],"formationLogic":"The name crossed several languages through biblical transmission; the stated Hebrew interpretation is the traditional name meaning.","mnemonic":null,"note":"这是人名的跨语言传递；词条录入小写不改变英文专名应大写的规则。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/Jesus"},contexts:[{"domain":"宗教史","senseId":"jesus.s1","en":"In the museum’s account of early Christianity, Jesus is presented as a first-century Jewish teacher whose life is central to Christian belief.","zh":"博物馆关于早期基督教的介绍将耶稣描述为一世纪的犹太教师，其生平是基督教信仰的核心。","structure":"whose 从句补充 teacher 的身份影响，前置短语限定介绍主题。","grammar":"Jesus 是专有名词，英文首字母大写；whose 引导关系从句。","rationale":"本句使用 jesus 词条中的基督教核心人物义，并保持宗教史陈述的中性语气。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The church’s stained-glass window depicts Jesus teaching a group of followers.','教堂的彩色玻璃窗描绘了耶稣向一群追随者讲道。')],mistakes:[m('The inscription names jesus as the central figure of Christianity.','The inscription names Jesus as the central figure of Christianity.','这里是基督教核心人物的专名，英语书写需将 Jesus 首字母大写。')],quiz:[q('jesus',1,1,'In Christianity, Jesus is?','the central figure of the religion','the name of a month','a term for a church building','来源义项说明 Jesus 是基督教的核心人物。'),q('jesus',2,1,'Which spelling is standard for the person’s name?','Jesus','jesus','JESUs','人名 Jesus 的标准书写首字母大写。'),q('jesus',3,1,'A passage about Jesus teaching mercy concerns?','a religious figure in Christianity','a type of sports shirt','a fast aircraft','Jesus 在词条中属于宗教人物义。'),q('jesus',4,1,'Which title is also associated with Jesus in Christian usage?','Christ','Jester','Jargon','来源词条列出的相关称谓之一是 Christ。')]});
D('jet',{etymology:{"origin":"The aircraft sense of jet arose from jet propulsion and jet engine; the older jet meant a stream or spurt, from French jet and jeter, to throw.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"The aircraft sense of jet arose from jet propulsion and jet engine; the older jet meant a stream or spurt, from French jet and jeter, to throw."}],"formationLogic":"The plane was named for its propulsion method, which in turn used the image of a forceful emitted stream.","mnemonic":null,"note":"Etymonline 记载其早期喷流义和后来的喷气飞机义。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/jet"},contexts:[{"domain":"航空技术","senseId":"jet.s1","en":"The airport introduced a quieter jet whose engines use less fuel during takeoff, although the aircraft still travels faster than the older propeller planes.","zh":"机场引进了一架噪声更小的喷气式飞机，其发动机在起飞时耗油更少，尽管它仍比旧式螺旋桨飞机飞得快。","structure":"whose 从句补充发动机特点，although 从句让步说明速度对比。","grammar":"jet 在此作名词指喷气式飞机；quieter 比较级与 less fuel 对照旧机型。","rationale":"词条的 jet 是由喷气发动机推进的飞机，而不只是任何高速飞机。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'A private jet crossed the mountains before landing at the coastal airport.','一架私人喷气式飞机飞越群山，随后降落在海岸机场。')],mistakes:[m('A jet crossed the sky under sail, powered only by a cloth sail and no engine.','A jet crossed the sky under engine power, using its jet engines.','jet 指喷气发动机驱动的飞机；只靠帆航行与之矛盾。')],quiz:[q('jet',1,1,'A passenger jet is?','an aircraft powered by jet engines','a train that travels on rails','a small boat powered by a sail','来源义项把 jet 定义为装有喷气发动机的飞机。'),q('jet',2,1,'The jet landed after a long flight. What landed?','a fast aircraft','a stream of water from a pipe','a piece of luggage','此处 jet 作名词，指喷气式飞机。'),q('jet',3,1,'Which phrase is natural?','a private jet','a jet of private','a privately jetting plane of','private jet 是表示私人喷气式飞机的自然短语。'),q('jet',4,1,'What can jet as a verb mean in ordinary usage?','to send out a narrow fast stream of liquid or gas','to travel only by walking','to close a door gently','词条注明 jet 的动词义为喷出。')]});
D('jetlag',{etymology:{"origin":"Jet lag, also written jetlag, is recorded from 1966 as jet in its airplane sense combined with lag, delay.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Jet lag, also written jetlag, is recorded from 1966 as jet in its airplane sense combined with lag, delay."}],"formationLogic":"The compound names the mismatch between the body’s timing and local time after rapid air travel.","mnemonic":null,"note":"jetlag 与分写 jet lag 均见资料；项目词头采用连写形式。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/jet lag"},contexts:[{"domain":"航空旅行","senseId":"jetlag.s1","en":"Although Mei slept during the overnight flight, the six-hour time difference left her with jet lag, so she postponed an important decision until morning.","zh":"尽管梅在夜航途中睡了觉，六小时的时差仍让她出现时差反应，因此她把一项重要决定推迟到早上。","structure":"although 让步说明睡眠没有消除影响，so 引出应对措施。","grammar":"jet lag 作不可数名词；leave someone with something 表示使某人出现某种状态。","rationale":"jet lag 指跨时区飞行后生物钟暂时错位造成的疲倦，不是单纯飞行劳累。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'After landing in Tokyo, she stayed awake until local evening to reduce the jetlag.','抵达东京后，她一直熬到当地傍晚，以减轻时差反应。')],mistakes:[m('He had jetlag after the long flight, so he felt fully rested and adjusted immediately to local time.','He had jetlag after the long flight, so he felt tired and needed time to adjust to local time.','jetlag 是长途飞行后出现的疲倦和时差不适；立刻完全休息好与之矛盾。')],quiz:[q('jetlag',1,1,'Jetlag is commonly felt after?','a long flight across time zones','a short walk to a nearby shop','a meal eaten at the usual local time','来源义项把 jetlag 解释为长途飞行后的疲乏。'),q('jetlag',2,1,'Someone with jetlag may have trouble?','sleeping at the local night-time','remembering how to walk','seeing any colours at all','跨时区后生物钟未调整会影响睡眠。'),q('jetlag',3,1,'Choose the natural sentence.','Jetlag made her tired the next day.','She jetlagged the suitcase into the room.','The jetlag were a new pair of shoes.','jetlag 是不可数名词，作句子主语可搭配 made。'),q('jetlag',4,1,'Which measure may help someone adjust after jetlag?','Follow the destination’s local sleep schedule.','Stay on the departure time forever.','Avoid all daylight at every hour.','按目的地作息帮助身体调整生物钟。')]});
