D('jetty',{etymology:{"origin":"Jetty came through Old French jetee, a pier or projecting structure, from the feminine past participle of jeter, to throw.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Jetty came through Old French jetee, a pier or projecting structure, from the feminine past participle of jeter, to throw."}],"formationLogic":"The name reflects a structure projected outward from the shore into the water.","mnemonic":null,"note":"词源所指为向水中伸出的建筑结构，不等于任意码头或海堤。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/jetty"},contexts:[{"domain":"港口设施","senseId":"jetty.s1","en":"Fishermen unloaded the baskets at the end of the jetty, where a small crane could lift them directly onto the shore road.","zh":"渔民在栈桥尽头卸下鱼筐，小型起重机可以在那里把鱼筐直接吊到岸边道路上。","structure":"where 从句补充说明栈桥尽头的设备功能。","grammar":"at the end of the jetty 标明卸货位置；them 回指 baskets。","rationale":"jetty 指伸入水面、供船只停靠或上下货物的平台。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'Passengers waited on the jetty while the small ferry approached the shore.','小渡船驶近岸边时，乘客们在栈桥上等候。')],mistakes:[m('The boat tied up at the jetty, a landing stage built into the water, miles inland on dry ground.','The boat tied up at the jetty, a landing stage built into the water beside the shore.','jetty 伸入水中供船只停靠；完全在内陆干地上无法供船停靠。')],quiz:[q('jetty',1,1,'A jetty is?','a landing stage that extends into the water','a road tunnel built under a mountain','a platform high above a railway station','jetty 指伸进水里的栈桥或码头。'),q('jetty',2,1,'Where would a boat normally tie up?','Alongside a jetty.','On top of a dry hill far from water.','Inside a passenger train.','栈桥位于水边，船可以靠泊在旁。'),q('jetty',3,1,'Choose the natural sentence.','We walked along the jetty to board the ferry.','We walked into the jetty to board the ferry.','We walked a jettyly to board the ferry.','along the jetty 表示沿栈桥行走。'),q('jetty',4,1,'A damaged jetty would most directly affect?','people boarding boats from the shore','aircraft taking off from an airport','cars passing through a road tunnel','栈桥的作用是供船只停靠和乘客上下船。')]});
D('jewel',{etymology:{"origin":"Jewel came through Anglo-French juel and Old French jouel; a possible source is Medieval Latin jocale, from Latin jocus, play or pastime, but the derivation is uncertain.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Jewel came through Anglo-French juel and Old French jouel; a possible source is Medieval Latin jocale, from Latin jocus, play or pastime, but the derivation is uncertain."}],"formationLogic":"The medieval forms are documented, while the proposed Latin explanation is one of several accounts.","mnemonic":null,"note":"Etymonline 将 jocale 关联标作可能解释，故明确记录不确定性。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/jewel"},contexts:[{"domain":"珠宝与保管","senseId":"jewel.s1","en":"The jeweller set the blue jewel in a plain silver mount so that the stone’s color, rather than the frame, would attract attention.","zh":"珠宝匠把蓝色宝石镶在朴素的银托上，好让人们注意宝石的颜色，而不是托架。","structure":"so that 从句说明设计目的，rather than 引出对照焦点。","grammar":"set a stone in a mount 是镶嵌搭配；would attract 表示预期效果。","rationale":"jewel 指镶嵌在托座中的珍贵宝石，本句区分宝石与金属托架。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The jeweller set the blue jewel in a silver ring for the exhibition.','珠宝商把这颗蓝宝石镶进银戒指，用于展览。')],mistakes:[m('The jeweller called the ordinary grain of sand a valuable jewel.','The jeweller called the precious stone set in the ring a valuable jewel.','jewel 指贵重宝石；普通沙粒不符合贵重宝石的定义。')],quiz:[q('jewel',1,1,'A jewel is usually?','a precious stone set in a piece of jewellery','a sheet of paper used as a label','a common stone found on every road','来源义项把 jewel 定义为镶嵌的贵重宝石。'),q('jewel',2,1,'A crown jewel is?','a valuable gem belonging to or set in a crown','a decorative paper crown for a child','a stone used to pave a road','crown jewel 是镶在王冠上的珍贵宝石，也可引申为最珍贵的部分。'),q('jewel',3,1,'Choose the natural phrase.','a jewel in a gold setting','a jewel into a gold settingly','a jewelled of gold setting','常说 a jewel in a setting，指镶在底座里的宝石。'),q('jewel',4,1,'Which word is closest in meaning to jewel here?','gem','receipt','fabric','jewel 的近义词包括 gem，均可指宝石。')]});
D('jig',{etymology:{"origin":"Jig as a lively dance is recorded in the sixteenth century; its origin is uncertain, though a link with Middle English gigge and Old French gigue, fiddle, has been suggested.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Jig as a lively dance is recorded in the sixteenth century; its origin is uncertain, though a link with Middle English gigge and Old French gigue, fiddle, has been suggested."}],"formationLogic":"The dance term may relate to an older fiddle or dance word, but sources do not settle the route.","mnemonic":null,"note":"历史联系仅为词源学者提出的可能路径。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/jig"},contexts:[{"domain":"舞蹈表演","senseId":"jig.s1","en":"The fiddler began a lively jig after the formal ceremony, and several guests clapped along before anyone dared to step onto the floor.","zh":"正式仪式结束后，提琴手开始演奏一支活泼的快步舞曲，几位宾客跟着拍手，随后才有人敢走上舞池。","structure":"after 和 before 连接舞曲开始、拍手和起舞的时间顺序。","grammar":"a jig 是舞蹈或舞曲名词；clap along 表示跟着节奏拍手。","rationale":"这里的 jig 指节奏轻快的舞蹈，不是工具名称或某些其他同形义。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The fiddler played a lively tune, and the guests danced a jig beside the fire.','小提琴手奏起欢快的曲子，客人们在炉火旁跳起快步舞。')],mistakes:[m('The programme describes a jig as a slow, solemn dance with no lively movement.','The programme describes a jig as a fast, lively dance.','来源义项将 jig 定义为欢快的快步舞；把它解释为缓慢沉闷的舞蹈不符。')],quiz:[q('jig',1,1,'A jig is?','a fast, lively dance','a slow formal speech','a type of cooking pot','来源义项将 jig 解释为欢快的快步舞。'),q('jig',2,1,'If the band plays a lively jig, dancers are likely to?','move quickly to the music','stand perfectly still for a silent ceremony','swim a race across the hall','jig 的特点是快而活泼，适合跳舞。'),q('jig',3,1,'Choose the natural phrase.','dance a jig','dance an equipment jig','dance jiggly a music','jig 是可数名词，可说 dance a jig。'),q('jig',4,1,'A jig is most closely connected with?','music and dancing','legal paperwork','road construction','jig 指一种舞蹈，常伴随音乐。')]});
D('jiggle',{etymology:{"origin":"Jiggle is an expressive formation from jig with the frequentative ending -le; the exact contribution of the ending is not fully certain, and jog may have influenced the form.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Jiggle is an expressive formation from jig with the frequentative ending -le; the exact contribution of the ending is not fully certain, and jog may have influenced the form."}],"formationLogic":"The extended form suggests repeated small movements rather than one large shake.","mnemonic":null,"note":"-le 的频繁义和 jog 的影响仅作词源解释，不将其分析为完全确定。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/jiggle"},contexts:[{"domain":"实验与测量","senseId":"jiggle.s1","en":"The technician had to jiggle the connector gently until the loose contact settled, taking care not to disturb the calibrated sensor beside it.","zh":"技术员不得不轻轻晃动连接器，直到松动的触点固定下来，同时小心不要碰动旁边校准过的传感器。","structure":"until 从句给出晃动停止的条件，taking care 补充操作注意事项。","grammar":"jiggle 是带小幅快速动作意味的动词；gently 修饰动作方式。","rationale":"jiggle 描述幅度小、连续短促的摇动，与不可扰动的精密传感器形成对照。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'She jiggled the handle gently until the stiff window latch moved.','她轻轻晃动把手，直到卡住的窗闩松动。')],mistakes:[m('He jiggled the key by keeping it completely still, without moving it at all.','He jiggled the key with small, quick movements until it turned.','jiggle 指小幅度快速摇晃；完全不动与该动作矛盾。')],quiz:[q('jiggle',1,1,'To jiggle a handle is to?','shake it with small quick movements','pull it once with a long steady force','paint it without touching it','jiggle 指以小幅度、快速地摇晃。'),q('jiggle',2,1,'Why might someone jiggle a stuck key?','To move it slightly until the lock turns.','To make the key disappear.','To measure how long the door is.','轻轻晃动卡住的钥匙可能让它转动。'),q('jiggle',3,1,'Choose the correct past form.','She jiggled the latch.','She jigled the latch.','She jiggling the latch yesterday.','jiggle 的过去式拼写为 jiggled，需双写 l。'),q('jiggle',4,1,'Which action is a jiggle rather than a steady pull?','quickly shaking a loose knob back and forth','pulling a rope smoothly for several minutes','lifting a box straight up without shaking','小幅度快速来回摇动最符合 jiggle。')]});
D('jingle',{etymology:{"origin":"Jingle is an imitative verb attested from the late fourteenth century; the noun for a light ringing sound developed from the verb.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Jingle is an imitative verb attested from the late fourteenth century; the noun for a light ringing sound developed from the verb."}],"formationLogic":"The sound pattern imitates a small ringing noise, later also naming the noise itself.","mnemonic":null,"note":"拟声性是词源资料明确提出的解释。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/jingle"},contexts:[{"domain":"声音描述","senseId":"jingle.s1","en":"A loose key began to jingle inside the desk drawer whenever the train rounded the curve, making the clerk look up from her notes.","zh":"火车每次转弯时，抽屉里一把松动的钥匙便叮当作响，使职员从笔记中抬起头来。","structure":"whenever 从句表示反复触发的时刻，making 短语交代声音产生的结果。","grammar":"jingle 在此作不及物动词；a loose key 是发声主体。","rationale":"jingle 表示轻快、连续的金属铃响，句中钥匙和火车震动共同产生这种声音。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'A light jingle came from the bells on the horse’s harness.','马具上的铃铛发出清脆的叮当声。')],mistakes:[m('The tiny bells made a jingle, but they produced no ringing sound at all.','The tiny bells made a jingle, producing a light ringing sound.','jingle 指清脆、轻快的铃声；完全没有铃声与前半句矛盾。')],quiz:[q('jingle',1,1,'A jingle is a?','light ringing sound','deep explosion','long stretch of silence','来源义项将 jingle 定义为清脆的轻响。'),q('jingle',2,1,'Coins in a pocket jingle when they?','make light ringing sounds as they move','turn into paper notes','remain perfectly still','硬币移动碰撞时会发出清脆的响声。'),q('jingle',3,1,'Which object is most likely to jingle?','a small bell on a collar','a thick carpet on a floor','a silent glass of water','小铃铛常会发出 jingle 声。'),q('jingle',4,1,'Choose the natural use as a verb.','The keys jingled in her bag.','The keys jingled the bag into a room.','The keys made a jinglingly bag.','jingle 可作不及物动词，描述发出清脆铃声。')]});
D('job',{etymology:{"origin":"Job meaning a piece of work is recorded in seventeenth-century English, with an uncertain origin and a possible relation to gob, a lump or mass; the paid-position sense came later.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Job meaning a piece of work is recorded in seventeenth-century English, with an uncertain origin and a possible relation to gob, a lump or mass; the paid-position sense came later."}],"formationLogic":"The modern employment sense developed from an earlier word for a task; its deeper origin remains uncertain.","mnemonic":null,"note":"gob 的关联只是可能解释，故不把它写成确证词根。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/job"},contexts:[{"domain":"就业与生活","senseId":"job.s1","en":"After finishing her degree, Aisha accepted a job at a regional clinic where she could use her language skills with patients.","zh":"艾莎毕业后接受了地区诊所的一份工作，在那里她可以用自己的语言能力与患者沟通。","structure":"after 介词短语交代时间背景，where 从句说明工作地点的特点。","grammar":"accept a job 表示接受一份有报酬的工作；where 回指 clinic。","rationale":"job 在此指持续的有薪工作，而不是临时任务或工作成果。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'Her first job after graduation was repairing bicycles at a neighborhood shop.','她毕业后的第一份工作是在社区店铺修自行车。')],mistakes:[m('She took a paid job, but received no wages for work she had already completed.','She took a paid job and received wages for the work she completed.','她已经完成工作却没有收到报酬，与 paid job 的含义冲突。')],quiz:[q('job',1,1,'A job in the source entry is?','regular paid work','a short holiday with no duties','a tool used to repair bicycles','来源义项把 job 定义为有报酬的固定工作。'),q('job',2,1,'Someone looking for a job is looking for?','paid employment','a new pair of shoes','a place to store old books','job 在职业语境中指工作或职位。'),q('job',3,1,'Choose the natural phrase.','apply for a job','apply a job for','apply into a job','apply for a job 是申请职位的自然搭配。'),q('job',4,1,'Which sentence correctly uses the countable noun?','She found a job near home.','She found job near home.','She found an jobs near home.','job 是可数名词，单数前需要 a/an 等限定词。')]});
D('jobless',{etymology:{"origin":"Jobless combines job with the negative suffix -less and is recorded in English from the late nineteenth century.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Jobless combines job with the negative suffix -less and is recorded in English from the late nineteenth century."}],"formationLogic":"The suffix means without, so the adjective describes someone without paid work.","mnemonic":null,"note":"job 的远源不确定；派生关系 job + -less 则透明。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/jobless"},contexts:[{"domain":"就业与社会保障","senseId":"jobless.s1","en":"The jobless engineer kept applying for positions while volunteering at a repair workshop to maintain practical skills and meet local employers.","zh":"这名失业工程师一边继续申请职位，一边在维修工坊做志愿者，以保持实操技能并结识当地雇主。","structure":"while 连接同时进行的求职和志愿活动，to maintain 表目的。","grammar":"jobless 由名词性成分和形容词后缀构成；keep applying 后接动名词。","rationale":"jobless 描述没有工作的状态，后文交代正在采取的求职措施。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The jobless engineer enrolled in a course while searching for a new position.','这名失业的工程师在寻找新职位的同时报名参加了一门课程。')],mistakes:[m('The jobless workers had secure jobs and were receiving regular pay.','The jobless workers had lost their jobs and were searching for work.','jobless 意为没有工作；有稳定工作和工资与之矛盾。')],quiz:[q('jobless',1,1,'A jobless person is?','without a job','working full-time in a paid position','retired after choosing not to work','jobless 表示失业、没有工作。'),q('jobless',2,1,'The number of jobless workers rose. This means more workers?','had no jobs','had received promotions','had moved into new offices','jobless workers 是失业工人。'),q('jobless',3,1,'In “the jobless need support,” the jobless refers to?','people who do not have jobs','people who own many companies','people who repair office desks','the + 形容词可指一类人；the jobless 指失业者。'),q('jobless',4,1,'Which word is closest in meaning to jobless?','unemployed','employed','self-employed with a full schedule','unemployed 表示失业，与 jobless 意义接近。')]});
D('jockey',{etymology:{"origin":"Jockey began as a Scottish familiar form Jockey of Jock, itself a Scottish form of Jack; the word broadened to mean a boy or fellow and later a race rider.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Jockey began as a Scottish familiar form Jockey of Jock, itself a Scottish form of Jack; the word broadened to mean a boy or fellow and later a race rider."}],"formationLogic":"A familiar personal name became a generic word for a young man, then specialized for a professional horse rider.","mnemonic":null,"note":"词源链保留 Jockey、Jock、Jack 的历史关系。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/jockey"},contexts:[{"domain":"赛马运动","senseId":"jockey.s1","en":"The jockey shortened his stirrups before the race because the muddy course required him to stay balanced through several sharp turns.","zh":"比赛前，骑师调短了马镫，因为泥泞的赛道要求他在几个急转弯中保持平衡。","structure":"because 从句说明调节装备的原因，through 短语说明平衡需要持续的赛段。","grammar":"the jockey 是骑手；require + object + to-infinitive 表示要求某人做某事。","rationale":"jockey 指骑赛马参加比赛的骑手，赛道条件解释了骑姿调整。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The jockey guided the horse around the final bend and toward the finish line.','骑师引导赛马绕过最后一个弯道，冲向终点线。')],mistakes:[m('The jockey rode in the horse race, but she never mounted or guided a horse.','The jockey rode and guided a horse during the race.','jockey 指赛马骑师；没有骑马或引导赛马的人不符合该职业定义。')],quiz:[q('jockey',1,1,'A jockey is a person who?','rides a horse in a race','judges a swimming competition','repairs the track after the race','jockey 指赛马比赛中的骑手。'),q('jockey',2,1,'During a race, a jockey’s role is to?','ride and guide the horse','sell tickets at the entrance','announce the weather forecast','骑师在比赛中骑乘并引导赛马。'),q('jockey',3,1,'Choose the natural phrase.','a professional jockey','a profession jockey','a jockeyly professional','professional 可作形容词修饰 jockey。'),q('jockey',4,1,'Which setting is most associated with a jockey?','a horse-racing track','a courtroom witness stand','a deep-sea research vessel','赛马场是 jockey 工作的典型场景。')]});
D('jog',{etymology:{"origin":"Jog first appears in the sixteenth century with a sense of moving or shaking up and down; its origin is uncertain, perhaps related to Middle English shoggen.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Jog first appears in the sixteenth century with a sense of moving or shaking up and down; its origin is uncertain, perhaps related to Middle English shoggen."}],"formationLogic":"The modern exercise sense is much later than the early motion verb, whose source remains unsettled.","mnemonic":null,"note":"shoggen 的联系仅为可能；此处不声称 jog 有已知单一词根。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/jog"},contexts:[{"domain":"健身与恢复","senseId":"jog.s1","en":"Because the doctor advised gradual exercise, Mei began to jog for ten minutes on level paths before increasing her distance each week.","zh":"因为医生建议循序渐进地锻炼，梅开始在平坦的小路上慢跑十分钟，然后每周增加距离。","structure":"because 从句交代训练原则，before 引出逐渐增加训练量的下一步。","grammar":"begin to jog 是不定式结构；before increasing 用动名词表示随后行动。","rationale":"jog 是为锻炼而缓慢跑步，十分钟和逐周增加体现低强度起步。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'I jog along the river path before breakfast three times a week.','我每周三次在早餐前沿河边步道慢跑。')],mistakes:[m('She jogged for exercise at a slow running pace, but she never ran or moved from her chair.','She jogged for exercise at a slow running pace around the park.','jog 指为锻炼而慢跑；一直坐着不动不可能完成慢跑。')],quiz:[q('jog',1,1,'To jog for exercise is to?','run at a slow, steady pace','sprint as fast as possible for one second only','walk backward without moving your legs','jog 指为锻炼而慢速跑步。'),q('jog',2,1,'Which plan includes a jog?','running slowly around the park before work','sitting at a desk and reading a map','cycling downhill at racing speed','慢跑是跑步的一种较慢形式。'),q('jog',3,1,'Choose the correct past form.','He jogged around the lake.','He joged around the lake.','He jogs around the lake yesterday.','jog 的过去式双写 g，再加 -ed：jogged。'),q('jog',4,1,'“Go for a jog” means?','go for a short or moderate run','go shopping for running shoes only','go to sleep after exercise','go for a jog 是去慢跑的自然表达。')]});
D('join',{etymology:{"origin":"Join came through Old French joindre from Latin iungere, to join or yoke together, from Proto-Indo-European *yeug-, to join.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Join came through Old French joindre from Latin iungere, to join or yoke together, from Proto-Indo-European *yeug-, to join."}],"formationLogic":"The historical root conveys putting things under one yoke or bringing them together.","mnemonic":null,"note":"原始印欧语重建形式按 Etymonline 记录。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/join"},contexts:[{"domain":"社团与报名","senseId":"join.s1","en":"Students who join the debate society before Friday will receive a schedule and may attend the first practice without paying a fee.","zh":"周五前加入辩论社的学生会收到日程表，并可免费参加第一次练习。","structure":"who 从句修饰 students，and 连接加入后获得的两项安排。","grammar":"join 后直接接团体名词作宾语，通常不加介词 to。","rationale":"join 表示成为组织成员，后续权益说明了入会结果。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'Several students joined the astronomy club after attending its first public meeting.','参加了天文学社第一次公开活动后，几名学生加入了社团。')],mistakes:[m('She joined to the chess club last week.','She joined the chess club last week.','表示成为团体成员时，join 是及物动词，直接接 club，不加 to。')],quiz:[q('join',1,1,'To join a club is to?','become one of its members','leave it permanently','watch it from outside without participating','join 的来源义项是成为某组织的一员。'),q('join',2,1,'Choose the standard construction.','join the team','join to the team','join with the team as a member of it','作“加入团队”解时 join 后直接接宾语。'),q('join',3,1,'Nina joined the committee in May. What happened?','She became a member of it.','She resigned from it.','She sold it to another group.','join the committee 表示加入委员会。'),q('join',4,1,'Which word is closest to join in “join a club”?','become a member of','separate from','argue against','在此用法中 join 意为成为……成员。')]});
D('join in',{etymology:{"origin":"Join in combines join, from Old French joindre and Latin iungere, with the particle in to express participation in an ongoing activity.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Join in combines join, from Old French joindre and Latin iungere, with the particle in to express participation in an ongoing activity."}],"formationLogic":"The particle gives join the sense of entering or sharing an activity already under way.","mnemonic":null,"note":"短语的历史说明依据 join 的词源和 in 的现代短语动词用法。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/join"},contexts:[{"domain":"集体活动","senseId":"join in.s1","en":"When the neighbors started singing at the community dinner, even the shy children joined in after their teacher began the familiar chorus.","zh":"社区晚餐上邻居们开始唱歌时，连害羞的孩子们也在老师唱起熟悉副歌后加入了合唱。","structure":"when 和 after 标出唱歌发起与孩子参与的先后关系。","grammar":"join in 是不及物短语动词，in 后不接活动宾语时可省略已知活动。","rationale":"join in 指参与已经进行的活动，句中孩子加入邻居们的歌唱。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'When the chorus began, even the shyest students joined in.','合唱开始时，连最腼腆的学生也参与进来。')],mistakes:[m('Everyone joined in the game, meaning they watched silently from outside and took no part.','Everyone joined in the game, meaning they took part with the others.','join in 意为参与；只在外面安静旁观并未参与。')],quiz:[q('join in',1,1,'To join in a game is to?','take part in it','own the building where it is played','stop it before anyone begins','join in 指参与某项活动。'),q('join in',2,1,'Which sentence uses join in naturally?','Would you like to join in the discussion?','Would you like to join the discussion in it?','Would you like to join in to the discussion?','join in 后可直接接活动名词；也可单独使用。'),q('join in',3,1,'The audience joined in the song. The audience?','sang along with the performers','left before the song began','wrote a review after the concert','join in the song 表示跟着一起唱。'),q('join in',4,1,'Which verb is closest to join in an activity?','participate','withdraw','observe silently','participate 表示参加活动，与 join in 接近。')]});
D('join up',{etymology:{"origin":"Join up combines join, from Old French joindre and Latin iungere, with up; the phrasal verb developed the sense of enlisting or formally joining a service.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Join up combines join, from Old French joindre and Latin iungere, with up; the phrasal verb developed the sense of enlisting or formally joining a service."}],"formationLogic":"The particle up marks completion or entry into the organized body in this established phrasal use.","mnemonic":null,"note":"join 的词源有明确拉丁链；join up 的具体搭配义属现代英语短语动词。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/join"},contexts:[{"domain":"军队招募","senseId":"join up.s1","en":"After discussing the risks with his family, Daniel decided to join up and completed the medical examination required of new recruits.","zh":"与家人讨论风险后，丹尼尔决定参军，并完成了新兵必须接受的体检。","structure":"after 短语交代决定背景，and 连接入伍决定后的手续。","grammar":"join up 是短语动词；decide to 后接不定式。","rationale":"join up 在此指加入军队成为新兵，而不是单纯把物件连接起来。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'After finishing school, he joined up and trained as a radio operator.','中学毕业后，他参军并接受了无线电操作员训练。')],mistakes:[m('He joined up with the army, but refused to enlist or become part of the service.','He joined up with the army and enlisted for service.','join up with the army 在该义中指参军；拒绝入伍与之矛盾。')],quiz:[q('join up',1,1,'In “She joined up after graduation,” joined up most likely means she?','enlisted in the armed forces','left the country permanently','joined a sports club as a spectator','join up 的来源义之一是参军、入伍。'),q('join up',2,1,'Which phrase clearly signals military service?','He joined up with the army.','He joined in the army’s concert as an audience member.','He joined the army’s office furniture.','join up with the army 表示参军。'),q('join up',3,1,'The roads join up at the bridge. What happens?','They meet or connect there.','They end on different continents.','They become a single vehicle.','来源还列出 join up 可指联合、连接起来。'),q('join up',4,1,'A person who joins up is most likely to?','become part of a military service','resign from every organization','watch a parade from home','join up 的典型义是应征入伍。')]});
D('joint',{etymology:{"origin":"Joint came through Old French joint from Latin iunctus, the past participle of iungere, to join; the related PIE root is *yeug-, join.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Joint came through Old French joint from Latin iunctus, the past participle of iungere, to join; the related PIE root is *yeug-, join."}],"formationLogic":"The anatomical noun developed from the idea of parts united at a meeting point; joint also has a related shared sense.","mnemonic":null,"note":"词源支持关节与连接的关系；未把词条的其他形容词义混进此句。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/joint"},contexts:[{"domain":"人体解剖","senseId":"joint.s1","en":"The physiotherapist showed Leo how to bend the knee joint without twisting the ankle, then asked him to repeat the movement slowly.","zh":"理疗师向利奥演示如何弯曲膝关节而不扭伤脚踝，然后让他慢慢重复这个动作。","structure":"how 从句说明演示内容，without 短语限制动作方式。","grammar":"knee 修饰 joint；ask + object + to-infinitive 表示要求某人重复动作。","rationale":"joint 指两块骨骼相接并活动的部位，膝关节例子与身体义项对应。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The physiotherapist checked the joint after the runner twisted her knee.','跑者扭伤膝盖后，理疗师检查了她的关节。'),ex(1,'The two charities issued a joint statement about the relief effort.','两家慈善机构就救援行动发表了一份联合声明。')],mistakes:[m('The doctors issued a joint statement, each writing a separate announcement and never working together.','The doctors issued a joint statement, preparing one announcement together.','joint 表示共同完成或共享；各自独立发布且没有合作与此相反。')],quiz:[q('joint',1,1,'A knee joint is the place where?','bones meet in the body','two roads cross in a city only','a muscle attaches to a shirt','joint 的名词义指骨骼相接的关节。'),q('joint',2,1,'A joint decision was made by two teams. It was made?','together by both teams','by one team without the other’s involvement','by a single person outside the teams','joint 作形容词时表示共同的、联合的。'),q('joint',3,1,'Choose the natural collocation.','a joint effort','a jointly effort','a join efforted','joint 是形容词，可修饰 effort。'),q('joint',4,1,'Painful stiffness in a joint affects?','a place where bones meet','the middle of a fingernail only','a person’s hearing','关节位于骨骼相接处。')]});
D('jointly',{etymology:{"origin":"Jointly is formed from joint, from Old French and Latin roots for joining, plus the adverb-forming suffix -ly.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Jointly is formed from joint, from Old French and Latin roots for joining, plus the adverb-forming suffix -ly."}],"formationLogic":"The adverb expresses that an action is carried out in a joined or shared manner.","mnemonic":null,"note":"派生关系 joint + -ly 透明，不需另设独立词根。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/jointly"},contexts:[{"domain":"合作与责任","senseId":"jointly.s1","en":"The two laboratories jointly analyzed the samples, and each team published its methods so that other researchers could reproduce the results.","zh":"两家实验室共同分析了样本，而且各团队都公布了方法，以便其他研究人员复现结果。","structure":"and 连接合作与公开方法，so that 表示公布方法的目的。","grammar":"jointly 修饰 analyzed；each team 后接单数 published。","rationale":"jointly 表示由双方共同完成，句子明确列出参与的两家实验室。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The two universities jointly funded a study on coastal erosion.','两所大学共同资助了一项海岸侵蚀研究。')],mistakes:[m('The two universities jointly funded the study, but each refused to contribute or cooperate.','The two universities jointly funded the study, and each contributed to it.','jointly funded 与双方都拒绝出资矛盾；right 说明两方都参与资助。')],quiz:[q('jointly',1,1,'If two organizations jointly fund a project, they fund it?','together','without knowing about it','only after the project has ended','jointly 表示和另一方共同进行。'),q('jointly',2,1,'Choose the correct word form: “They ___ own the building.”','jointly','joint','jointness','动词 own 需要副词 jointly 修饰，表示共同拥有。'),q('jointly',3,1,'A report written jointly by two researchers was written?','by both researchers together','by neither researcher','by one researcher’s employer alone','jointly 强调多方一起完成。'),q('jointly',4,1,'Which phrase is closest in meaning to jointly?','together with another','separately from everyone','by accident only','jointly 的来源释义是 together with another。')]});
D('joke',{etymology:{"origin":"Joke was borrowed in the 1660s from Latin iocus, jest or pastime, and was initially colloquial English.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Joke was borrowed in the 1660s from Latin iocus, jest or pastime, and was initially colloquial English."}],"formationLogic":"A Latin word for playful speech or amusement entered English as the modern noun and verb.","mnemonic":null,"note":"不将 joke 和 jest 的相近历史形式混同。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/joke"},contexts:[{"domain":"团队沟通","senseId":"joke.s1","en":"The manager opened the meeting with a gentle joke about the broken coffee machine, then moved quickly to the urgent safety report.","zh":"经理以一个关于坏掉咖啡机的温和玩笑开场，随后迅速转入紧急安全报告。","structure":"with 短语说明开场方式，then 标出会议议程的转折。","grammar":"open a meeting with something 表示以某事开场；about 引出笑话主题。","rationale":"joke 指旨在逗笑或轻松气氛的言语内容，gentle 限定其友善程度。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'His joke about the missing cake made the whole team laugh.','他关于蛋糕不见了的笑话逗得全队大笑。')],mistakes:[m('She told a joke to make everyone laugh, but the remark was a serious legal instruction.','She told a joke to make everyone laugh, and the remark was not meant as a serious instruction.','joke 是为了逗笑的话；严肃的法律指令不是笑话。')],quiz:[q('joke',1,1,'A joke is something said or done to?','make people laugh','measure a person’s height','close a bank account','来源义项将 joke 定义为让人发笑的内容。'),q('joke',2,1,'Choose the natural phrase for teasing someone playfully.','play a joke on a friend','play a joke at a friend','play a joking of a friend','play a joke on someone 是自然搭配。'),q('joke',3,1,'If people laugh at a joke, they find it?','funny','airtight','unwritten','笑话通常意在逗笑，因此 funny 对应其用途。'),q('joke',4,1,'Which sentence uses joke as a verb?','They joked about the weather.','They joke was about the weather.','They made a jokeing about the weather.','joke 可作动词，表示开玩笑或说笑。')]});
D('joker',{etymology:{"origin":"Joker was formed from joke with the agent suffix -er; Etymonline records the person-who-jokes sense in the eighteenth century.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Joker was formed from joke with the agent suffix -er; Etymonline records the person-who-jokes sense in the eighteenth century."}],"formationLogic":"The English suffix names a person characterized by the activity expressed in joke.","mnemonic":null,"note":"仅取该词条支持的开玩笑者义，不扩展到其他后起用法。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/joker"},contexts:[{"domain":"同事相处","senseId":"joker.s1","en":"Everyone knew Ravi as the office joker, but he became serious whenever a customer described a problem that could affect their safety.","zh":"大家都知道拉维是办公室里爱开玩笑的人，但只要顾客提到可能影响安全的问题，他就会严肃起来。","structure":"but 表示玩笑形象与工作态度的对照，whenever 表示反复出现的条件。","grammar":"the office joker 是名词短语；whenever 从句限定 became serious 的时机。","rationale":"joker 指喜欢开玩笑的人，而非扑克牌中的 joker 或不可靠的人。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'Our team’s joker lightened the mood during the long overnight shift.','我们团队里爱开玩笑的人缓和了漫长夜班的气氛。')],mistakes:[m('The joker was known for making the group laugh, but she never joked or tried to amuse anyone.','The joker was known for making the group laugh with jokes and playful remarks.','joker 指爱开玩笑、逗乐的人；从不说笑或逗人不符合定义。')],quiz:[q('joker',1,1,'A joker in a group is someone who?','likes to joke and make people laugh','enforces every rule without speaking','repairs playing cards for a living','来源义项把 joker 解释为爱开玩笑的人。'),q('joker',2,1,'Which person is most likely to be called the group’s joker?','the one who often makes playful remarks','the one who never speaks to anyone','the one who records the meeting minutes','常说俏皮话、逗大家笑的人符合 joker。'),q('joker',3,1,'Choose the correct plural.','two jokers','two jokies','two joker','joker 的规则复数形式是 jokers。'),q('joker',4,1,'A joker may help a tense group by?','using humour to lighten the mood','hiding all the chairs','canceling every conversation','爱开玩笑的人可能用幽默缓和气氛。')]});
D('jolly',{etymology:{"origin":"Jolly came through Old French jolif, meaning festive or merry; the older origin of the French form is uncertain.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Jolly came through Old French jolif, meaning festive or merry; the older origin of the French form is uncertain."}],"formationLogic":"The recorded borrowing supports the cheerful sense, while the deeper source remains unresolved.","mnemonic":null,"note":"不沿用项目旧注中缺少依据的日耳曼语词根说法。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/jolly"},contexts:[{"domain":"节日与氛围","senseId":"jolly.s1","en":"Despite the long queue and cold rain, the volunteers stayed jolly as they handed hot soup to families waiting outside the shelter.","zh":"尽管队伍很长、雨水冰冷，志愿者们递热汤给在收容所外等候的家庭时仍保持愉快。","structure":"despite 介词短语表达逆境，as 从句说明保持愉快时正在做的事情。","grammar":"stay + 形容词描述持续状态；as 引导伴随时间从句。","rationale":"jolly 表示快乐、开朗，句中志愿者在困难条件下仍显得友善。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The jolly host welcomed the guests with a broad smile and a cheerful greeting.','快乐热情的主人笑容满面地欢迎客人。')],mistakes:[m('She was jolly, meaning cheerful and happy, but she was not cheerful or happy at all.','She was jolly, meaning cheerful and happy.','jolly 表示愉快、开朗；wrong 对这个词的解释与词义直接矛盾。')],quiz:[q('jolly',1,1,'A jolly person is?','cheerful and happy','angry and unwilling to speak','physically unable to move','来源义项把 jolly 定义为愉快、开朗的。'),q('jolly',2,1,'Which description best fits a jolly celebration?','people laugh and enjoy themselves','everyone is silent and deeply unhappy','the building is empty and locked','jolly 可形容欢快愉悦的气氛。'),q('jolly',3,1,'Choose the natural phrase.','a jolly old man','a jollily old man','a jolliness old man','jolly 是形容词，可直接修饰 man。'),q('jolly',4,1,'Which word is closest to jolly?','cheerful','jealous','jobless','cheerful 表示愉快开朗，与 jolly 接近。')]});
D('jolt',{etymology:{"origin":"Jolt is recorded from the late sixteenth century; proposed links to Middle English jollen or obsolete jot exist, but its origin is uncertain.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Jolt is recorded from the late sixteenth century; proposed links to Middle English jollen or obsolete jot exist, but its origin is uncertain."}],"formationLogic":"The word’s abrupt sound and motion fit its meaning, yet no single historical derivation is established.","mnemonic":null,"note":"音义联想不等于已证拟声词源，保留来源未定。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/jolt"},contexts:[{"domain":"交通与安全","senseId":"jolt.s1","en":"A deep pothole gave the bus a sharp jolt, waking the sleeping child before the driver could slow down near the school gate.","zh":"公交车猛地颠了一下，把睡着的孩子惊醒了，司机还没来得及在校门附近减速。","structure":"分词短语 waking 说明颠簸造成的结果，before 从句限定司机减速时间。","grammar":"give someone a jolt 是名词搭配；could slow down 表示尚未来得及做到。","rationale":"jolt 是突然而粗猛的震动，坑洼路面对公交车造成这种震动。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The bus hit a pothole and gave every passenger a sudden jolt.','公交车撞上一个坑洼，所有乘客都猛地颠了一下。')],mistakes:[m('The bus gave the passengers a jolt, but they felt no sudden shake at all.','The bus gave the passengers a jolt, and they felt a sudden shake.','jolt 就是突然的摇晃；right 的两个分句保持一致。')],quiz:[q('jolt',1,1,'A jolt on a bumpy road is?','a sudden rough shake','a smooth and motionless ride','a gentle sound from a radio','jolt 的名词义是突然的剧烈颠簸或晃动。'),q('jolt',2,1,'If a loud bang jolts someone, it?','shocks or startles them suddenly','helps them fall asleep peacefully','makes them walk more slowly by choice','jolt 作动词可表示突然震动或使人吃惊。'),q('jolt',3,1,'Choose the natural phrase.','a sudden jolt','a suddenly jolt','a joltly movement','形容词 sudden 修饰名词 jolt。'),q('jolt',4,1,'Which event is most likely to give a car a jolt?','hitting a deep pothole','standing still in a garage','being washed gently by hand','撞上深坑会造成突然颠簸。')]});
D('jostle',{etymology:{"origin":"Jostle developed from jousten or justle with the frequentative suffix -le; joust came through Old French joster from Latin iuxta, beside.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Jostle developed from jousten or justle with the frequentative suffix -le; joust came through Old French joster from Latin iuxta, beside."}],"formationLogic":"The form shifted from meeting or colliding in a joust to repeated pushing in a crowd.","mnemonic":null,"note":"来源链和频繁后缀解释依据 Etymonline。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/jostle"},contexts:[{"domain":"拥挤场景","senseId":"jostle.s1","en":"Passengers jostled one another near the train doors as they tried to board before the warning bell sounded.","zh":"乘客们在车门附近互相推挤，想赶在警示铃响起前上车。","structure":"as 从句说明推挤发生的背景，before 引出登车的时间限制。","grammar":"jostle one another 表示相互推挤；try to 后接不定式。","rationale":"jostle 指在人群中推挤，车门处的拥挤和抢着上车构成具体情景。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'Commuters jostled for space as the crowded train doors opened.','拥挤列车车门打开时，通勤者们互相推挤着争抢空间。')],mistakes:[m('The passengers jostled in the crowd without touching or pushing anyone.','The passengers jostled in the crowd, pushing against one another for room.','jostle 指在人群中推挤；wrong 却说无人被碰撞或推挤。')],quiz:[q('jostle',1,1,'To jostle people in a crowd is to?','push or bump against them','sit far away from them in silence','ask them to leave by written notice','jostle 指在人群中推挤、挤撞。'),q('jostle',2,1,'The fans jostled for a better view. They?','pushed and crowded as they competed for a place','stood in a quiet line with no competition','left the stadium before the match','jostle for 表示推挤争抢某物或位置。'),q('jostle',3,1,'Choose the natural preposition in this phrase.','jostle for position','jostle at positionly','jostle to of position','jostle for a place/position 是常见搭配。'),q('jostle',4,1,'Which situation best illustrates jostling?','passengers bumping shoulders in a packed doorway','friends sitting apart in an empty park','a boat floating without touching the dock','拥挤门口肩膀相撞体现 jostle。')]});
D('journal',{etymology:{"origin":"Journal came through Anglo-French jurnal and Old French jornel, a day or day’s work, from Late Latin diurnalis, daily, and Latin dies, day.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Journal came through Anglo-French jurnal and Old French jornel, a day or day’s work, from Late Latin diurnalis, daily, and Latin dies, day."}],"formationLogic":"The word’s daily association led from a day’s record to a personal diary and later to periodicals.","mnemonic":null,"note":"Etymonline 给出的演变包含日记和期刊等后续义。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/journal"},contexts:[{"domain":"个人记录","senseId":"journal.s1","en":"Nora wrote in her journal each evening, noting one decision she regretted and one small success she wanted to remember.","zh":"诺拉每天晚上都在日记中写下自己后悔的一项决定，以及想要记住的一件小小成功。","structure":"noting 伴随 wrote，后面的两个并列成分具体说明日记内容。","grammar":"write in a journal 是常见搭配；she regretted 和 she wanted 修饰各自名词。","rationale":"journal 在此是每日记录个人经历的日记，不是学术期刊。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'She records the route, weather, and small discoveries in a travel journal.','她在旅行日记中记录路线、天气和沿途的小发现。'),ex(1,'The researchers submitted their findings to a medical journal.','研究人员把研究结果提交给了一本医学期刊。')],mistakes:[m('She wrote each day’s observations in her journal, but the notebook contained no daily records at all.','She wrote each day’s observations in her journal, keeping a daily record of the trip.','journal 作日记时是每日记录；声称完全没有日常记录与前句矛盾。')],quiz:[q('journal',1,1,'A travel journal can be?','a written record of a person’s trip','a ticket used to board a train','a map that cannot contain notes','journal 的来源义之一是每天或持续写下的记录。'),q('journal',2,1,'A medical journal is?','a publication that carries professional articles','a private diary used only by one patient','a hospital’s emergency room','journal 也可指学术或专业期刊。'),q('journal',3,1,'Choose the natural phrase for keeping a personal record.','keep a journal','keep journally','keep a journaling of','keep a journal 是记日记的自然搭配。'),q('journal',4,1,'Researchers publish an article in a journal to?','share findings in a periodical publication','keep the article secret from all readers','replace every laboratory instrument','学术期刊用于发表和传播研究文章。')]});
