D('journalism',{etymology:{"origin":"Journalism entered English from French journalisme, formed from journal, and is recorded in the early nineteenth century.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Journalism entered English from French journalisme, formed from journal, and is recorded in the early nineteenth century."}],"formationLogic":"The suffix -ism names a practice or professional sphere built around the journal and news work.","mnemonic":null,"note":"词源显示它与 journal 的记录、报刊义相连。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/journalism"},contexts:[{"domain":"新闻传播","senseId":"journalism.s1","en":"Because the editor had worked in journalism for decades, she asked the trainee to separate verified facts from anonymous speculation before publication.","zh":"由于编辑从事新闻工作已有数十年，她要求实习生在发表前将核实过的事实与匿名猜测分开。","structure":"because 从句说明编辑经验，before 从句给出核查必须完成的时间点。","grammar":"work in journalism 指从事新闻业；ask + object + to-infinitive 表示要求。","rationale":"journalism 指新闻报道和写作这一职业领域，核实事实是此领域的核心工作。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'She chose journalism because she wanted to investigate local decisions and report them clearly.','她选择新闻业，是因为想调查当地决策并清楚地报道出来。')],mistakes:[m('He studied journalism so he could write and report news, but his course had nothing to do with news work.','He studied journalism so he could write and report news, which is central to news work.','journalism 指新闻采写工作；学习它却与新闻工作毫无关系会造成语义矛盾。')],quiz:[q('journalism',1,1,'Journalism is?','the work of gathering and writing news','the study of repairing musical instruments','the legal process of choosing a judge','来源义项把 journalism 定义为新闻采写工作。'),q('journalism',2,1,'A student studying journalism is preparing to?','report and write news stories','design bridges without collecting information','serve food at a restaurant','journalism 与报道、写作新闻有关。'),q('journalism',3,1,'Choose the natural phrase.','a career in journalism','a journalism of career','a career journalismly','in journalism 是表示从事新闻工作的自然搭配。'),q('journalism',4,1,'Which task is most clearly journalism?','interviewing residents and writing a news report','copying a shopping list into a diary','deciding a court case as a judge','采访并报道新闻属于 journalism。')]});
D('journalistic',{etymology:{"origin":"Journalistic is formed from journalist with the adjectival suffix -ic and means characteristic of journalism or journalists.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Journalistic is formed from journalist with the adjectival suffix -ic and means characteristic of journalism or journalists."}],"formationLogic":"The suffix makes an adjective describing the style or practices associated with journalism.","mnemonic":null,"note":"这是透明的派生形态；不另假设独立词根。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/journalistic"},contexts:[{"domain":"媒体写作","senseId":"journalistic.s1","en":"The report used a journalistic style, placing the strongest verified detail in the opening paragraph and explaining its sources near the end.","zh":"这篇报道采用新闻写作风格，把最有力且已核实的细节放在首段，并在结尾附近说明消息来源。","structure":"placing 和 explaining 组成伴随分词结构，分别说明写作安排。","grammar":"journalistic 修饰 style；the strongest verified detail 用最高级限定核心信息。","rationale":"journalistic 表示具有新闻报道特征，句中展示了信息排序和来源说明。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The article uses a concise journalistic style, with the key facts in its opening paragraph.','这篇文章采用简洁的新闻写作风格，在开头段落交代了关键信息。')],mistakes:[m('Her journalistic style was clear and suited to reporting, but it had no connection with journalism.','Her journalistic style was clear and suited to journalism.','journalistic 表示与新闻业或新闻写作有关；说它与新闻业无关自相矛盾。')],quiz:[q('journalistic',1,1,'A journalistic style is a style connected with?','journalism and news writing','jewellery design','judicial sentencing','journalistic 的意思是新闻的、新闻写作的。'),q('journalistic',2,1,'Which piece of writing is most likely to have a journalistic style?','a clear news report about a city decision','a recipe written only as a poem','a private code with no readers','新闻报道最可能采用 journalistic style。'),q('journalistic',3,1,'Choose the correct form before “writing.”','journalistic writing','journalism writingly','journalist writingness','journalistic 是修饰 writing 的形容词。'),q('journalistic',4,1,'A journalistic article usually aims to?','report information clearly to readers','hide all relevant facts from readers','replace a court ruling with a joke','journalistic 与报道信息、新闻写作有关。')]});
D('journalists',{etymology:{"origin":"Journalists is the regular plural of journalist, formed from journal with the agent suffix -ist; the singular word is recorded from the late seventeenth century.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Journalists is the regular plural of journalist, formed from journal with the agent suffix -ist; the singular word is recorded from the late seventeenth century."}],"formationLogic":"The plural ending -s marks multiple people whose work is connected with journals or news reporting.","mnemonic":null,"note":"journalist 的构词链由 journal 与 -ist 支持；此处复数为常规屈折。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/journalist"},contexts:[{"domain":"新闻采访","senseId":"journalists.s1","en":"The journalists waited outside the hearing room until the judge released a written decision that they could quote accurately.","zh":"记者们在听证室外等候，直到法官发布书面裁决，使他们能够准确引用。","structure":"until 从句标出等候结束的时间，that 从句修饰 decision。","grammar":"journalists 是 journalist 的规则复数；they 回指多名记者。","rationale":"journalists 指从事新闻采集和报道的人，等待正式文件以便引用体现其工作。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'Journalists waited outside the council building for the mayor’s announcement.','记者们在市政厅外等候市长的公告。')],mistakes:[m('The journalists wrote reports about the event, but every one of the reporters refused to write or report anything.','The journalists wrote reports about the event, and the reporters filed their stories.','journalists 指从事新闻写作的人；说他们都拒绝报道与前半句冲突。')],quiz:[q('journalists',1,1,'Journalists are people who?','write or report news','decide every court case','repair engines on trains','journalists 是记者，负责采写新闻。'),q('journalists',2,1,'A group of journalists at a press conference will most likely?','ask questions and report the answers','serve as the conference’s security guards','replace the speakers on stage','记者在发布会上通常采访并报道信息。'),q('journalists',3,1,'Which verb agrees with the plural subject?','The journalists are waiting outside.','The journalists is waiting outside.','The journalists waits outside.','journalists 是复数主语，谓语用 are。'),q('journalists',4,1,'Journalists filed a story before the deadline. They?','submitted a news report','closed the courthouse','registered a new company','journalist 指写新闻的人，file a story 指提交报道。')]});
D('journey',{etymology:{"origin":"Journey came through Old French journée, a day’s length or day’s travel, from Vulgar Latin *diurnum and Latin diurnus, of a day, related to dies, day.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Journey came through Old French journée, a day’s length or day’s travel, from Vulgar Latin *diurnum and Latin diurnus, of a day, related to dies, day."}],"formationLogic":"The word began with the notion of a day’s travel and broadened to travel between places generally.","mnemonic":null,"note":"星号表示重建形式，并非直接存世的拉丁词形。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/journey"},contexts:[{"domain":"出行计划","senseId":"journey.s1","en":"The journey from the island clinic to the mainland hospital took six hours because the ferry had to wait for the storm to pass.","zh":"从岛上诊所到大陆医院的旅程花了六个小时，因为渡船必须等风暴过去。","structure":"from...to... 给出行程两端，because 从句说明耗时原因。","grammar":"the journey from A to B 描述两地之间的旅程；take + 时间表示耗时。","rationale":"journey 指从一地到另一地的行程，句中给出起点、终点和时长。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The overnight journey by train gave us time to read and rest.','乘火车过夜的旅程让我们有时间阅读和休息。')],mistakes:[m('Their journey from the station to the hotel covered a distance, but they never travelled between the two places.','Their journey from the station to the hotel involved travelling between the two places.','journey 是从一处到另一处的行程；没有发生移动就没有完成这段旅程。')],quiz:[q('journey',1,1,'A journey is?','travel from one place to another','a permanent address','a type of travel document','journey 指从一处到另一处的行程。'),q('journey',2,1,'Which phrase is natural?','a long journey by train','a journey at the train','a journey of trainly','journey by train 表示乘火车进行的旅程。'),q('journey',3,1,'They began their journey at dawn. What began?','Their travel from one place to another.','Their permanent stay in one room.','Their court hearing.','journey 的核心义是旅行、行程。'),q('journey',4,1,'Choose the correct countable form.','We had a tiring journey.','We had tiring journey.','We had an journeys.','journey 是可数名词，单数需要 a/an 等限定词。')]});
D('joust',{etymology:{"origin":"Joust came through Old French joster from Vulgar Latin *iuxtare, based on Latin iuxta, beside or near; its deeper connection with PIE *yeug-, join, is proposed.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Joust came through Old French joster from Vulgar Latin *iuxtare, based on Latin iuxta, beside or near; its deeper connection with PIE *yeug-, join, is proposed."}],"formationLogic":"The verb originally carried the idea of coming alongside or meeting, later specializing in mounted combat.","mnemonic":null,"note":"远源与 PIE 的联系采用词典中标注的推测语气。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/joust"},contexts:[{"domain":"中世纪历史","senseId":"joust.s1","en":"Two armored riders prepared to joust before the crowd, lowering their lances only after the marshal gave the agreed signal.","zh":"两名身披盔甲的骑手准备在观众面前比武，直到主裁发出约定信号后才放低长矛。","structure":"only after 强调动作必须等到信号之后，before 短语说明表演场景。","grammar":"prepare to joust 后接不定式；lowering 是伴随动作，only after 突出时间顺序。","rationale":"joust 指骑马持长矛相斗的比武，本句交代了骑手、长矛和开始信号。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The performers jousted on horseback with padded lances at the historical festival.','历史节庆上，表演者骑在马上用包软垫的长矛比武。')],mistakes:[m('The knights jousted on horseback with lances, while both riders remained on foot throughout the contest.','The knights jousted on horseback with lances, riding toward one another during the contest.','joust 是骑马用长矛比武；说骑士全程都步行与之矛盾。')],quiz:[q('joust',1,1,'A traditional joust is a contest in which riders?','fight on horseback with lances','race boats across a lake','compete by solving legal cases','joust 指骑马用长矛进行的比武。'),q('joust',2,1,'In a joust, the participants traditionally carry?','lances','tennis rackets','fishing nets','长矛是传统 joust 中使用的武器。'),q('joust',3,1,'Which sentence uses joust as a verb?','The knights jousted at the festival.','The knights joust was on horseback.','The knights jousting a festival.','joust 可作动词，表示骑马持矛比武。'),q('joust',4,1,'A jousting match is most likely part of?','a historical reenactment','a swimming lesson','a court appeal hearing','joust 与中世纪骑士比武相关。')]});
D('joy',{etymology:{"origin":"Joy came through Old French joie from Latin gaudia or gaudium, joy, from gaudere, to rejoice; the root is associated with rejoicing.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Joy came through Old French joie from Latin gaudia or gaudium, joy, from gaudere, to rejoice; the root is associated with rejoicing."}],"formationLogic":"The French borrowing preserved the noun meaning a feeling of gladness or delight.","mnemonic":null,"note":"不额外断言有争议的更深 PIE 词根。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/joy"},contexts:[{"domain":"家庭与情感","senseId":"joy.s1","en":"The letter brought her joy because it confirmed that her brother had safely arrived after weeks without any news from him.","zh":"这封信给她带来了喜悦，因为它证实失联数周的弟弟已平安抵达。","structure":"because 从句解释喜悦来源，that 从句是 confirmed 的内容。","grammar":"bring someone joy 是固定搭配；after weeks without news 表示此前的等待。","rationale":"joy 指强烈的愉悦感，安全消息解决了担忧，因此带来喜悦。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The children shouted with joy when their father returned home.','父亲回家时，孩子们高兴地喊了起来。')],mistakes:[m('She accepted the award with joy, but she felt no pleasure or happiness at all.','She accepted the award with joy and felt great pleasure.','joy 指强烈的愉悦感；完全没有快乐与该情绪矛盾。')],quiz:[q('joy',1,1,'Joy is a feeling of?','great pleasure and happiness','physical pain in a joint','confusion about a schedule','joy 指欢乐、极大的愉悦感。'),q('joy',2,1,'Someone receives news with joy when they feel?','very happy about it','angry that it happened','unable to understand it','with joy 表示带着喜悦。'),q('joy',3,1,'Choose the natural phrase.','full of joy','full with joyness','a joy of full','full of joy 是常见搭配。'),q('joy',4,1,'Which word is closest to joy?','delight','jealousy','jargon','delight 表示快乐、欣喜，与 joy 意义接近。')]});
D('joyful',{etymology:{"origin":"Joyful combines joy, from Old French joie and Latin gaudium, with the English adjective-forming suffix -ful.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Joyful combines joy, from Old French joie and Latin gaudium, with the English adjective-forming suffix -ful."}],"formationLogic":"The suffix means full of, producing an adjective for someone or something characterized by joy.","mnemonic":null,"note":"joy + -ful 是有依据的英语派生构词。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/joyful"},contexts:[{"domain":"庆祝活动","senseId":"joyful.s1","en":"Although the ceremony was brief, the joyful families stayed in the garden afterward to share food and photographs with the graduates.","zh":"尽管仪式很简短，满怀喜悦的家人们随后仍留在花园里，与毕业生分享食物和照片。","structure":"although 引导让步从句，afterward 标出仪式之后的庆祝活动。","grammar":"joyful 作定语修饰 families；stay + place 表示继续留在某处。","rationale":"joyful 表示充满喜悦，语境中的家庭庆祝具体呈现了这种情绪。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'It was a joyful reunion, with cousins laughing together after many years apart.','那是一次欢乐的团聚，分别多年的表亲们一起笑着交谈。')],mistakes:[m('They had a joyful reunion and felt full of happiness, but the event was completely miserable.','They had a joyful reunion and felt full of happiness.','joyful 意为充满喜悦；说团聚完全令人痛苦与前文矛盾。')],quiz:[q('joyful',1,1,'A joyful occasion is?','full of happiness','full of legal arguments','without any participants','joyful 表示充满喜悦、令人愉快。'),q('joyful',2,1,'Which event is most likely to be joyful?','a long-awaited family reunion','a machine failing during an emergency','a court denying every appeal','久别重逢通常会是 joyful 的场合。'),q('joyful',3,1,'Choose the correct phrase.','a joyful celebration','a joyfully celebration','a joyfulness celebration','joyful 是形容词，可修饰 celebration。'),q('joyful',4,1,'Joyful is closest in meaning to?','glad','jolted','jobless','glad 表示高兴，与 joyful 接近。')]});
D('judge',{etymology:{"origin":"Judge came through Old French juge or juger from Latin iudex or iudicare; iudex is often analyzed as ius, law, plus the root of dicere, to say.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Judge came through Old French juge or juger from Latin iudex or iudicare; iudex is often analyzed as ius, law, plus the root of dicere, to say."}],"formationLogic":"The historical formation is glossed as one who declares the law; the verb later broadened to forming opinions.","mnemonic":null,"note":"拉丁构词分析由词源词典支持，此处不将现代 judge 随意拆词。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/judge"},contexts:[{"domain":"法院程序","senseId":"judge.s1","en":"The judge listened to both witnesses, compared their accounts with the recorded evidence, and postponed the ruling until the following morning.","zh":"法官听取了两名证人的陈述，将他们的说法与记录在案的证据进行比较，并把裁决推迟到次日早晨。","structure":"三个并列谓语体现法官依次采取的行动。","grammar":"judge 作名词指司法裁决者；listen to 后接对象，compare A with B。","rationale":"此处 judge 是法院中的法官，审听证词和证据并推迟裁决是其职责。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The judge listened to both sides before giving a decision in court.','法官在作出裁决前听取了双方陈述。')],mistakes:[m('The judge heard both sides and issued a court ruling, but the person was not involved in deciding the case.','The judge heard both sides and issued a court ruling, deciding the case.','法官的职责包括裁决案件；说此人没有参与决定与前面行为矛盾。')],quiz:[q('judge',1,1,'A judge in a court is a person who?','hears cases and makes legal decisions','writes weather forecasts','repairs the courthouse roof','judge 作名词指法院中的裁决者。'),q('judge',2,1,'To judge a competition is to?','evaluate the entries and decide their results','compete without any evaluation','sell tickets at the entrance','judge 作动词可表示评判或作出判断。'),q('judge',3,1,'Choose the natural phrase.','judge from the evidence','judge at the evidencely','judge of from the evidence','judge from 表示根据某证据作判断。'),q('judge',4,1,'The judge ruled in her favor. What did the judge do?','made a court decision supporting her','joined her team as a player','wrote a private diary entry','judge 可指作出法律裁决的法官。')]});
D('judgement',{etymology:{"origin":"Judgement is the British spelling variant of judgment, from Old French jugement, an action of trying at law or the capacity to decide, related to jugier, to judge.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Judgement is the British spelling variant of judgment, from Old French jugement, an action of trying at law or the capacity to decide, related to jugier, to judge."}],"formationLogic":"The noun developed from the French verb for judging; the extra e is a conventional spelling variant, not a different derivation.","mnemonic":null,"note":"英美拼写变体都有效；本句采用题头给出的 judgement。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/judgement"},contexts:[{"domain":"决策能力","senseId":"judgement.s1","en":"Good judgement led the captain to delay departure when the forecast worsened, even though the crew had already loaded the supplies.","zh":"天气预报转差时，良好的判断力使船长决定推迟出发，尽管船员已经装好了物资。","structure":"when 从句给出判断发生的情境，even though 表示延误带来的不便。","grammar":"judgement 作不可数抽象名词；lead someone to do 表示促使某人采取行动。","rationale":"judgement 指基于信息作出明智决策的能力，船长据预报调整计划。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'Good judgement helped the pilot turn back before the storm became dangerous.','良好的判断力让飞行员在风暴变得危险前掉头返航。')],mistakes:[m('Her judgement are usually sound when the evidence is clear.','Her judgement is usually sound when the evidence is clear.','judgement 表示判断力时可作单数抽象名词，谓语应使用 is。')],quiz:[q('judgement',1,1,'Good judgement is the ability to?','make sensible decisions','hear sounds more clearly','write a court’s final ruling only','judgement 的来源义项是作出好决定的能力。'),q('judgement',2,1,'A person with sound judgement is likely to?','consider the facts before deciding','ignore all evidence','change a decision every few seconds','sound judgement 指可靠、明智的判断力。'),q('judgement',3,1,'Which spelling is standard in British English?','judgement','judgiment','judgemant','judgement 是常见英式拼写；美式通常写 judgment。'),q('judgement',4,1,'Choose the correct agreement.','Her judgement is valued by the team.','Her judgement are valued by the team.','Her judgements is valued by the team.','这里 judgement 作单数抽象名词，谓语用 is。')]});
D('judges',{etymology:{"origin":"Judges is the regular plural of judge, which came through Old French juge from Latin iudex, one who declares the law.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Judges is the regular plural of judge, which came through Old French juge from Latin iudex, one who declares the law."}],"formationLogic":"The ending -s marks more than one judicial officer; the shared historical base is judge.","mnemonic":null,"note":"只记录复数屈折；法官一词的词源见 judge。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/judge"},contexts:[{"domain":"法院与案件","senseId":"judges.s1","en":"The judges entered the courtroom together after the clerk announced that all parties were present and the hearing could begin.","zh":"书记员宣布各方均已到场、听证会可以开始后，几位法官一同走进法庭。","structure":"after 从句交代法官入庭前的程序通知，that 从句列出宣布内容。","grammar":"judges 是 judge 的规则复数；all parties were present 与 hearing could begin 并列。","rationale":"judges 在此指多名审理案件的法官，复数形式由上下文明确。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The judges compared each performance before announcing the final scores.','评委们比较了每场表演后才宣布最终分数。')],mistakes:[m('The judges compared the performances and announced their scores, but there was only one judge.','The judges compared the performances and announced their scores as a panel.','judges 是 judge 的复数；若只有一位，不能用 judges。')],quiz:[q('judges',1,1,'Judges in a competition are people who?','evaluate performances or entries','perform every entry themselves','sell food to the audience','judges 可指负责评判比赛的评委。'),q('judges',2,1,'In a court, judges are?','people who decide legal cases','the people accused in every case','the reporters covering a hearing','judges 也可指法官，judge 的复数。'),q('judges',3,1,'Which verb agrees with judges?','The judges have reached a decision.','The judges has reached a decision.','The judges reaches a decision.','judges 是复数，搭配 have。'),q('judges',4,1,'What is the correct singular form of judges?','judge','judg','judgeses','judges 是 judge 的复数形式。')]});
D('judgment',{etymology:{"origin":"Judgment comes through Old French jugement, an act of trying at law or a court decision, from jugier, to judge; English also has the variant spelling judgement.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Judgment comes through Old French jugement, an act of trying at law or a court decision, from jugier, to judge; English also has the variant spelling judgement."}],"formationLogic":"The legal noun developed from the act of judging into the authoritative result of that process.","mnemonic":null,"note":"避免将 judgment 和 judgement 当作语义不同的词；二者主要是拼写差异。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/judgment"},contexts:[{"domain":"司法裁决","senseId":"judgment.s1","en":"After reviewing the contracts and hearing both sides, the court issued a judgment requiring the company to repay the disputed deposit.","zh":"审阅合同并听取双方陈述后，法院作出判决，要求公司退还有争议的押金。","structure":"after reviewing 和 hearing 列出裁决前的程序，requiring 分词说明判决内容。","grammar":"issue a judgment 是法院作出裁决；requiring 表示裁决附带的义务。","rationale":"judgment 指法院正式作出的裁决，而不是仅仅个人判断力。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The court’s judgment was published after the appeal had been heard.','上诉审理结束后，法院公布了裁决。')],mistakes:[m('The court issued its judgment, a decision in the case, but it made no decision at all.','The court issued its judgment, a decision in the case.','judgment 指法院作出的决定；称其为裁决却说完全没有决定相矛盾。')],quiz:[q('judgment',1,1,'A court judgment is?','a decision given by a court','a judge’s lunch break','a list of witnesses’ home addresses','judgment 的来源义是法院作出的裁决。'),q('judgment',2,1,'If a judgment is appealed, a party?','asks a higher court to review the decision','asks the judge to join a jury','cancels the entire legal system','上诉通常是请求更高法院审查裁决。'),q('judgment',3,1,'Which spelling is also accepted in British English for the legal noun?','judgement','judjment','judgemente','judgement 是 judgment 的英式拼写变体，两者都正确。'),q('judgment',4,1,'Choose the natural phrase.','the court’s judgment','the court’s judgmenting','a court judgmently','judgment 是可数名词，可说 a court judgment。')]});
D('judicial',{etymology:{"origin":"Judicial came from Latin iudicialis, belonging to a court, from iudicium, judgment or court, and iudex, judge; iudex relates ius, law, to dicere, say.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Judicial came from Latin iudicialis, belonging to a court, from iudicium, judgment or court, and iudex, judge; iudex relates ius, law, to dicere, say."}],"formationLogic":"The adjective marks matters belonging to a court or the administration of justice.","mnemonic":null,"note":"词源中 ius 加 dicere 的解释记录为历史构词分析。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/judicial"},contexts:[{"domain":"司法制度","senseId":"judicial.s1","en":"The commission recommended judicial review of the detention policy so that an independent court could test whether officials had followed the law.","zh":"委员会建议对拘留政策进行司法审查，使独立法院能够检验官员是否依法行事。","structure":"so that 从句说明建议审查的目的，whether 从句作 test 的宾语。","grammar":"judicial 修饰 review，表示与法院或司法程序有关；could test 表示审查能力。","rationale":"judicial 表示与法官、法院和司法管理有关，司法审查是典型搭配。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The judicial process gave both parties time to present evidence.','司法程序给了双方陈述证据的时间。')],mistakes:[m('The judicial process concerned the courts and judges, but it had nothing to do with the legal system.','The judicial process concerned the courts, judges, and legal system.','judicial 表示司法的、与法院法官有关；说它与法律体系毫无关系矛盾。')],quiz:[q('judicial',1,1,'A judicial process is connected with?','courts and judges','fruit juice production','sports uniforms','judicial 指与法院、法官有关的司法事务。'),q('judicial',2,1,'A judicial system includes?','courts and the processes for applying law','only the country’s weather stations','a network of train junctions','judicial system 指司法体系。'),q('judicial',3,1,'Choose the natural collocation.','judicial review','judicially reviewment','judgment reviewful','judicial review 是司法审查的自然搭配。'),q('judicial',4,1,'Which word is closest in meaning to judicial?','legal','jolly','jealous','legal 表示法律的，与 judicial 接近。')]});
D('judiciary',{etymology:{"origin":"Judiciary entered English as an adjective from Latin iudiciarius, belonging to a court; the collective noun for judges as a body is recorded from 1788.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Judiciary entered English as an adjective from Latin iudiciarius, belonging to a court; the collective noun for judges as a body is recorded from 1788."}],"formationLogic":"The adjective meaning court-related was later used collectively for the judicial branch or its judges.","mnemonic":null,"note":"词条兼具形容词和集合名词历史；语境选择名词义。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/judiciary"},contexts:[{"domain":"政府与司法","senseId":"judiciary.s1","en":"The constitution protects the judiciary from direct political control, allowing judges to decide cases according to law rather than party pressure.","zh":"宪法保护司法机构免受直接政治控制，使法官能够依法裁案，而不受党派压力左右。","structure":"allowing 分词说明制度保护产生的效果，rather than 引出对照依据。","grammar":"the judiciary 是集合名词，指一国的法官群体或司法机关；allow + object + to-infinitive。","rationale":"judiciary 指作为整体的法官系统，句中通过独立裁案说明其制度角色。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The judiciary is expected to apply the law independently of political pressure.','司法机构应不受政治压力影响，独立适用法律。')],mistakes:[m('The judiciary is the body of a country’s judges, but it contains no judges at all.','The judiciary is the body of a country’s judges, considered as a group.','judiciary 指一国法官整体；说其中没有法官与定义直接冲突。')],quiz:[q('judiciary',1,1,'A country’s judiciary is?','its judges considered as a body','its elected sports teams','its network of public libraries','judiciary 指一国法官组成的整体、司法系统。'),q('judiciary',2,1,'If the judiciary upholds a ruling, the judges?','support or maintain the decision','write a newspaper article about it only','cancel every court hearing','uphold a ruling 是司法机构维持裁决。'),q('judiciary',3,1,'The judiciary is usually treated as?','a collective institution','a plural of judicial','one individual judge only','来源说明 judiciary 常作单数集合名词。'),q('judiciary',4,1,'Which phrase is natural?','an independent judiciary','a judicially judiciary','a judiciary of independents only','independent judiciary 是自然搭配，表示独立司法机构。')]});
D('juice',{etymology:{"origin":"Juice came through Old French jus from Latin ius, broth, sauce, or juice; the deeper PIE connection with mixing food is uncertain.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Juice came through Old French jus from Latin ius, broth, sauce, or juice; the deeper PIE connection with mixing food is uncertain."}],"formationLogic":"The Latin food liquid term narrowed in English to the liquid extracted from fruit or vegetables.","mnemonic":null,"note":"更深 PIE 联系属词源提议，不写作定论。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/juice"},contexts:[{"domain":"烹饪与营养","senseId":"juice.s1","en":"The chef squeezed fresh lemon juice over the grilled vegetables just before serving, adding acidity without making the herbs lose their flavor.","zh":"厨师在上桌前把新鲜柠檬汁挤在烤蔬菜上，增加酸味而没有盖过香草的味道。","structure":"just before serving 指明添加时间，without 引出未发生的副作用。","grammar":"juice 作物质名词；squeeze juice over something 表示把汁挤淋在食物上。","rationale":"juice 指水果中的液体，此处明确由柠檬挤出并用于调味。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'Fresh orange juice was served with breakfast after the harvest festival.','丰收节后的早餐供应了鲜榨橙汁。')],mistakes:[m('She squeezed the oranges and served their juice, but the glass contained no liquid from the fruit.','She squeezed the oranges and served the liquid from the fruit as juice.','juice 指水果中的液体；若玻璃杯里没有果汁，就不应说供应了这种 juice。')],quiz:[q('juice',1,1,'Fruit juice is?','the liquid obtained from fruit','the hard outer shell of a fruit','the seed inside every fruit','来源义项将 juice 解释为水果里的液体。'),q('juice',2,1,'A glass of apple juice contains?','liquid from apples','pieces of paper shaped like apples','a whole apple tree','juice 可指从苹果等水果中榨取的液体。'),q('juice',3,1,'Choose the natural phrase.','a glass of juice','a glass of juices for one drink','a juice of glass','通常说 a glass of juice，juice 作物质名词。'),q('juice',4,1,'Which verb naturally combines with juice?','squeeze fresh juice from an orange','hammer juice into an orange','fold juice into a paper envelope','可从橙子中 squeeze 榨出果汁。')]});
D('jul',{etymology:{"origin":"Jul is the conventional short calendar form of July; the full month name came from Latin Iulius through Anglo-French and Old French forms.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Jul is the conventional short calendar form of July; the full month name came from Latin Iulius through Anglo-French and Old French forms."}],"formationLogic":"The clipped form saves space in dates, while the historical origin belongs to the complete month name.","mnemonic":null,"note":"这是日期书写缩写，不是独立古词源；完整词 July 以罗马人名命名。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/July"},contexts:[{"domain":"日历缩写","senseId":"jul.s1","en":"The project timeline lists the review as Jul 8, while the signed contract spells out July to prevent confusion for international partners.","zh":"项目进度表将评审日期写作7月8日，而签署的合同拼出完整 July，以免国际合作方产生歧义。","structure":"while 对照进度表中的缩写形式与合同中的完整形式。","grammar":"Jul 是 July 的常用月份缩写；spell out 表示不用缩写而写出全词。","rationale":"本句展示 jul 在日历日期中的缩写功能，也提醒正式合同可写全称。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The archive box is labelled “Jul 2019,” indicating the month of the photograph.','档案盒上标着“Jul 2019”，说明照片拍摄的月份。')],mistakes:[m('The date stamp reads “Jul 12,” and the note says the event took place in January.','The date stamp reads “Jul 12,” and the note says the event took place in July.','Jul 是 July 的月份缩写；写着 Jul 12 却说事件发生在 January，月份不一致。')],quiz:[q('jul',1,1,'On a calendar, Jul is short for?','July','June','January','jul/Jul 是 July 的缩写。'),q('jul',2,1,'Which date uses the normal capitalization?','Jul 12','jul 12','JULy 12','月份缩写通常首字母大写，写作 Jul。'),q('jul',3,1,'A schedule says “Jul–Aug.” Which months are meant?','July and August','June and April','January and August','Jul 指 July，Aug 指 August。'),q('jul',4,1,'Which full month does “Jul.” abbreviate?','July','June','January','Jul. 是 July 的常见缩写。')]});
D('July',{etymology:{"origin":"July came through Anglo-French julie and Old French Juil from Latin Iulius; the Roman month was renamed for Julius Caesar, who was born in it.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"July came through Anglo-French julie and Old French Juil from Latin Iulius; the Roman month was renamed for Julius Caesar, who was born in it."}],"formationLogic":"The earlier Roman name Quintilis meant fifth because the old calendar began in March.","mnemonic":null,"note":"词条明确说明当前月份序号与罗马旧历名称序号不同。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/July"},contexts:[{"domain":"历法与季节","senseId":"July.s1","en":"The observatory opens late in July because the meteor shower is easiest to watch after midnight, when the sky is darkest.","zh":"天文台在七月下旬延长开放时间，因为午夜后、天空最暗时最容易观测流星雨。","structure":"because 解释延长开放的原因，when 从句修饰观测条件。","grammar":"in July 表示月份；late in July 指月末；after midnight 作时间状语。","rationale":"July 是一年的第七个月，句中作为季节和活动时间标记。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The outdoor theatre opens its summer season in July.','露天剧院在七月开启夏季演出季。')],mistakes:[m('The calendar marks July as the sixth month of the year.','The calendar marks July as the seventh month of the year.','July 是一年的第七个月，不是第六个月。')],quiz:[q('July',1,1,'July is the ___ month of the year.','seventh','sixth','twelfth','July 是一年的第七个月。'),q('July',2,1,'Which preposition is natural for a month?','in July','on July','at July','月份名前通常使用 in。'),q('July',3,1,'A festival is held in July. When is it held?','During the year’s seventh month.','During the year’s sixth month.','During the year’s first month.','July 对应第七个月。'),q('July',4,1,'Which abbreviation commonly stands for July?','Jul.','Jun.','Jan.','Jul. 是 July 的月份缩写。')]});
D('jump',{etymology:{"origin":"Jump appears in English in the sixteenth century with no clear Old or Middle English source; an imitative origin has been proposed, but its deeper source is uncertain.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Jump appears in English in the sixteenth century with no clear Old or Middle English source; an imitative origin has been proposed, but its deeper source is uncertain."}],"formationLogic":"The modern verb’s historical origin is unresolved; sound or motion imitation is only a proposal.","mnemonic":null,"note":"不把项目旧注中未证实的词根分析沿用为事实。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/jump"},contexts:[{"domain":"体育训练","senseId":"jump.s1","en":"At the final whistle, the goalkeeper had to jump sideways to reach the ball before it crossed the line into the net.","zh":"终场哨响前，守门员必须向侧面跃起，在球越过球门线前将它拦下。","structure":"before 从句说明跃起和触球必须赶在球过线之前。","grammar":"jump 后接方向副词 sideways；have to 表示必须。","rationale":"jump 指双脚蹬地或身体突然跃起，守门员为扑球而侧向腾空。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The child jumped over a shallow puddle on the way home.','孩子回家路上跳过了一个浅水坑。')],mistakes:[m('She jumped by pushing off the ground, but both feet stayed firmly on the ground throughout.','She jumped by pushing off the ground, briefly lifting both feet into the air.','jump 指蹬地腾空；双脚始终牢牢踩地没有跳起来。')],quiz:[q('jump',1,1,'To jump is to?','push off the ground and move into the air','lie still without moving','slide along the ground without lifting the body','来源义项将 jump 定义为蹬地跳起。'),q('jump',2,1,'The cat jumped onto the table. What did it do?','leapt up onto the table','dug a tunnel under the table','walked around the room without approaching it','jump onto 表示跳到某物上面。'),q('jump',3,1,'Choose the correct past tense.','They jumped across the stream.','They jumpded across the stream.','They jump across the stream yesterday.','jump 的过去式为 jumped。'),q('jump',4,1,'Which noun phrase refers to an athletics event?','the long jump','the long jumpingly','a jump of longness','long jump 是跳远项目的名称。')]});
D('jun',{etymology:{"origin":"Jun is the conventional short calendar form of June, whose English name came from Latin Iunius, probably meaning sacred to Juno.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Jun is the conventional short calendar form of June, whose English name came from Latin Iunius, probably meaning sacred to Juno."}],"formationLogic":"The abbreviation is a modern clipping used in dates; the historical month-name origin is Latin.","mnemonic":null,"note":"完整月名与 Juno 的关联带有 probably，不进一步断言神名更深来源。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/June"},contexts:[{"domain":"日历缩写","senseId":"jun.s1","en":"The archive labels the folder Jun 2022, but its catalog entry gives the full month name so that readers can search by either form.","zh":"档案把文件夹标为2022年6月，但目录条目写出完整月份名称，方便读者用两种形式检索。","structure":"but 对比文件夹标签与目录条目，so that 表目的。","grammar":"Jun 是 June 的常用月份缩写；either form 指缩写和全称两种写法。","rationale":"本句把 jun 放在年月格式中，显示它作为月份缩写使用。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The invitation is dated “Jun 14,” the usual abbreviation for the month.','请柬日期写作“Jun 14”，这是该月份的常见缩写。')],mistakes:[m('The ticket says “Jun 14,” but the itinerary states that the train leaves in December.','The ticket says “Jun 14,” and the itinerary states that the train leaves in June.','Jun 是 June 的缩写；日期标为 Jun 14 却写成 December，月份信息不一致。')],quiz:[q('jun',1,1,'In a date, Jun is short for?','June','January','July','jun/Jun 是 June 的缩写。'),q('jun',2,1,'Which form uses normal capitalization?','Jun 14','jun 14','JUNe 14','月份缩写首字母大写，写作 Jun。'),q('jun',3,1,'A plan says “May–Jun.” Which two months are included?','May and June','May and July','March and January','Jun 表示 June，即六月。'),q('jun',4,1,'Which abbreviation corresponds to June?','Jun.','Jul.','Jan.','Jun. 是 June 的常见日期缩写。')]});
D('junction',{etymology:{"origin":"Junction comes from Latin iunctionem, a joining, formed from the past-participle stem of iungere, to join, from PIE *yeug-, join.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Junction comes from Latin iunctionem, a joining, formed from the past-participle stem of iungere, to join, from PIE *yeug-, join."}],"formationLogic":"The place sense developed from the action of joining into the point where routes meet.","mnemonic":null,"note":"拉丁语 iungere 与英语 join 同源，原始印欧词根按词源词典列出。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/junction"},contexts:[{"domain":"交通路线","senseId":"junction.s1","en":"At the junction of the two rural roads, a new sign directs heavy trucks away from the school and toward the bypass.","zh":"在两条乡间道路的交汇处，一块新路牌引导重型卡车避开学校、驶向绕行道。","structure":"介词短语 At the junction 定位地点，主句说明路牌的指向。","grammar":"junction of A and B 表示两条路线汇合处；direct A away from B toward C。","rationale":"junction 指道路相交或汇合的地点，本句直接给出两条路和交通功能。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'Turn left at the junction where the two country roads meet.','在两条乡间公路交汇的路口左转。')],mistakes:[m('The two railway lines met at a junction, but they remained separate and never connected there.','The two railway lines met and connected at a junction.','junction 指线路相接的地方；两条线从未连接就不构成该交汇点。')],quiz:[q('junction',1,1,'A road junction is a place where?','roads or routes meet','one road ends in the middle of an empty field with no connection','a river flows beneath a bridge without crossing a road','junction 是道路或线路相交、连接的地方。'),q('junction',2,1,'At a railway junction, passengers may need to?','change to another line','board a boat at a harbour','leave the train to cross an airport runway','铁路 junction 是线路交汇处，可在此换乘。'),q('junction',3,1,'Choose the natural phrase.','a busy road junction','a junctionly road','a road junctioning of','road junction 是道路交汇处的自然搭配。'),q('junction',4,1,'Which word is closest to junction in a road map?','intersection','journal','javelin','intersection 指道路交叉口，与 junction 接近。')]});
D('June',{etymology:{"origin":"June came through Old French and Anglo-French forms from Latin Iunius, probably a contraction of Iunonius, sacred to Juno.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"June came through Old French and Anglo-French forms from Latin Iunius, probably a contraction of Iunonius, sacred to Juno."}],"formationLogic":"The Roman month name was adopted into English; the proposed expansion of Iunius remains qualified as probable.","mnemonic":null,"note":"不将 Juno 或 Iunius 的更早来源写成确定事实。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/June"},contexts:[{"domain":"历法与季节","senseId":"June.s1","en":"By June, the mountain snow had begun to melt, so the ranger reopened the upper trail but kept warning signs near the unstable bridge.","zh":"到了六月，山上的积雪开始融化，因此护林员重新开放了上段步道，但仍在不稳固的桥边保留警示牌。","structure":"By June 设定时间界限，so 表示融雪带来的开放决定，but 表示安全保留措施。","grammar":"by June 表示不迟于六月；had begun 是过去完成时，先于 reopening。","rationale":"June 是一年的第六个月，季节变化用其作时间背景。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The university’s summer term ends in June, just before the student move-out week.','大学的夏季学期在六月结束，紧接着是学生搬离周。')],mistakes:[m('June is the sixth month, but the planner labels it as the seventh month of the year.','June is the sixth month, and the planner labels it as the sixth month of the year.','June 是一年的第六个月；把它标为第七个月是错误的。')],quiz:[q('June',1,1,'June is the ___ month of the year.','sixth','seventh','first','June 是一年的第六个月。'),q('June',2,1,'Choose the natural phrase for an event during June.','in June','on June','at June','月份前通常使用介词 in。'),q('June',3,1,'The exams finish in June. When do they finish?','During the year’s sixth month.','During the year’s seventh month.','During the year’s last month.','June 对应第六个月。'),q('June',4,1,'Which abbreviation commonly stands for June?','Jun.','Jul.','Jan.','Jun. 是 June 的日期缩写。')]});
